00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:53.660
As a person.
作为一个人来说。

173
00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.180
I remember his rehearsal.
我记得他的排练。

174
00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.140
We had gotten sort of lazy in our blocking.
我们当时在走位上有点懒散了。

175
00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.280
You know, we're like, oh, I go up to reception.
你知道，我们就像是，哦，我走到前台。

176
00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:01.860
I stand here.
我站在这里。

177
00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:02.680
I'm at the copier.
我在复印机旁。

178
00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.180
I get it.
我明白了。

179
00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:03.960
I look over there.
我往那边看一眼。

180
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:09.260
And then our first day rehearsing with him, he had like a visual map in his brain.
然后我们和他排练的第一天，他脑子里就像有一张视觉地图。

181
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.340
You could see he'd walk over.
你能看到他走过去。

182
00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.880
He'd say, then I pick up my glasses.
他说，然后我拿起眼镜。

183
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.220
Then I set my notebook down.
然后我放下笔记本。

184
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.400
Then I take two steps.
然后我走两步。

185
00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.800
And he was going through this process.
他正在经历这个过程。

186
00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.400
I pick up my glasses on this line.
我在这句台词时拿起眼镜。

187
00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.820
And that's when I'm going to put them on.
然后我就要戴上它们。

188
00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.840
And I'm going to look that way.
然后我要看向那个方向。

189
00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:20.150
Yeah.
没错。

190
00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.340
And then when we decided to do it again, he went back to a starting spot.
然后当我们决定再来一次时，他回到了起始位置。

191
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.960
But like in reverse, like this part indeed means everything.
就像倒带一样，这一部分确实意义重大。

192
00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.640
He went through each step backwards.
他把每一步都倒着做了一遍。

193
00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:30.100
Yeah.
没错。

194
00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:30.780
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

195
00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:37.100
I thought his interview as Robert California in this episode was just brilliant.
我觉得他在这一集中饰演罗伯特·加利福尼亚的面试表现简直绝了。

196
00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:42.060
That was, you know, you can debate, was Robert California right for the show?
那是，你知道，你可以争论，罗伯特·加利福尼亚是否适合这部剧？

197
00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.500
You know, you can debate that.
你知道，你可以争论这一点。

198
00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.140
I think he brought a lot of great stuff to the show.
但我认为他为这部剧带来了很多很棒的东西。

199
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:50.520
And he's a stellar talent that I have loved for 30 years.
他是一位我喜爱了30年的杰出天才。

200
00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.840
But that interview was amazing.
但那场面试真是太棒了。

201
00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.720
His job interview in this episode was absolutely incredible.
他在这一集里的面试表现简直绝了。

202
00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:58.520
It was.
确实。

203
00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.200
You're never selling something.
你卖的从来都不是产品。

204
00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.200
You're selling sex.
你卖的是性。

205
00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:01.820
Right, Toby?
对吧，托比？

206
00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.420
And Toby's like, yeah.
然后托比就说，没错。

207
00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:04.060
Yeah.
没错。

208
00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:05.980
It's so good.
太棒了。

209
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.560
Well, we loved how you as Dwight interviewed yourself.
嗯，我们很喜欢你以德怀特的身份面试自己的那段。

210
00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:10.260
Yeah.
是啊。

211
00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.600
I actually think we should play it, Jenna.
我觉得我们应该放出来听听，珍娜。

212
00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:13.780
Okay.
好啊。

213
00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.660
If you're not going to interview me, then I'll do it.
如果你不打算面试我，那我就自己来。

214
00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:15.940
Yes.
好。

215
00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.760
What will be your first priority?
你的首要任务是什么？

216
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.560
I will have seven first priorities.
我会有七个首要任务。

217
00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:23.600
Safety.
安全。

218
00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:24.860
Profits.
利润。

219
00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:28.540
Fostering a community of self-reliance and entrepreneurship.
培养自力更生和创业精神的社区。

220
00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:29.700
Listening.
倾听。

221
00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.920
Respect for human life.
尊重生命。

222
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.120
Bolstering our public image.
提升我们的公众形象。

223
00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:37.020
And getting everyone home on time.
还有让大家准时下班。

224
00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.920
Dwight, let me be frank.
德怀特，我直说了吧。

225
00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.820
In an accident that no one can blame you for, an antique gun was discharged while you were acting manager.
在你担任代理经理期间，发生了一起你无法推卸责任的事故，一把古董枪走火了。

226
00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.180
How are we ever to trust you again?
我们怎么还能再信任你呢？

227
00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.580
Great question.
问得好。

228
00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:57.580
I am going to institute a strict no firearms policy for this office that extends to myself as well.
我打算在办公室实行严格的禁枪政策，我也包括在内。

229
00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.620
Wow.
哇。

230
00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.840
All of my concerns are disappearing.
我所有的顾虑都消失了。

231
00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.020
Thank you, Dwight.
谢谢你，德怀特。

232
00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:02.980
Thank you.
谢谢。

233
00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.550
You'll be hearing from us shortly, Mr. Schrute.
我们很快会联系你的，施鲁特先生。

234
00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.730
And I think you're going to like the call you're going to receive.
我想你会喜欢接到的那个电话的。

235
00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.430
Oh, come on.
噢，得了吧。

236
00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.250
I'm just happy that I got this meeting.
我能得到这次面试机会就已经很高兴了。

237
00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.230
It's so well written.
这剧本写得太好了。

238
00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:21.430
When you got the script, did you just get so excited about getting to do that?
当你拿到剧本时，是不是因为能演这段而感到特别兴奋？

239
00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:22.910
A couple of things.
有几件事。

240
00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:28.770
So this script, I had two comedy, situational comedy geMs.
关于这个剧本，我有两个情景喜剧的瑰宝。

241
00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:32.170
The Jacques Souvenet interview with the burn victim.
一个是雅克·苏维内采访烧伤受害者的那段。

242
00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:33.930
And this self-interview.
另一个就是这段自我面试。

243
00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:40.370
And I remember just being gleefully ecstatic at this possibility.
我记得当时想到这个可能性时，简直欣喜若狂。

244
00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:47.710
I think the Jacques Souvenet, there is a, you know, if Dave Rogers is doing supersized episodes and longer episodes, I think there is a much longer,
我觉得雅克·苏维内那段，你知道，如果戴夫·罗杰斯做超长版剧集的话，我觉得应该还有一段更长、

245
00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:51.190
much funnier Jacques Souvenet extended scene.
更好笑的雅克·苏维内加长戏份。

246
00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.250
Because I remember that going on for a long time.
因为我记得那段拍了很久。

247
00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:56.290
And us laughing and finding so much stuff.
我们当时笑个不停，还挖掘出了很多东西。

248
00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.490
And they, because they have to chop everything down.
但因为他们必须把所有内容剪短。

249
00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.410
And it ended up being, you know, 47 seconds.
最后只剩下了47秒。

250
00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:03.450
But there's a couple minutes of really good stuff in there.
但里面其实还有几分钟非常精彩的内容。

251
00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:08.570
And then taking a step back, I think one of the things I greatly appreciate about the show, looking back on it now,
退一步来看，我觉得现在回首这部剧，我非常欣赏的一点是，

252
00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:14.630
is there's a classic comedy element to The Office that's often overlooked.
《办公室》里有一种常被忽视的经典喜剧元素。

253
00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:24.490
Like physical comedy and kind of comedy setups that kind of come from almost like Commedia dell'arte or vaudeville of like,
比如肢体喜剧，还有那种几乎源自意大利即兴喜剧或杂耍表演的喜剧桥段，就是那种，

254
00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:27.790
how do we create a situation in which this little kind of nugget,
我们该如何创造一个情境，让这种小小的“金块”，

255
00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:35.170
like the Jacques Souvenet burn victim interview can happen within the context of these characters that we know and love.
比如雅克·苏维内那个烧伤受害者采访，能够在我们熟悉并喜爱的角色背景下自然发生。

256
00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.150
I mean, it's, it's as old as sitcoms themselves, this idea.
我的意思是，这个想法和情景喜剧本身一样古老。

257
00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:43.490
But the writers would consistently give me stuff like that.
但编剧们总是会给我写出那样的东西。

258
00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:51.970
That was, when I look back on the show, some of the stuff comedically that I savor the most was the amazing stuff that gave Dwight, like Dwight fighting himself.
当我回看这部剧时，我最享受的喜剧片段之一，就是那些给德怀特设计的精彩内容，比如德怀特自己打自己。

259
00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:52.510
Yes.
没错。

260
00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:52.870
You know?
你知道吗？

261
00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:53.210
Yes.
是的。

262
00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:57.030
It's just, it's a brilliant, these are brilliant little setups.
这真是太棒了，这些都是非常精彩的小桥段。

263
00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:00.170
I don't know how else to, they're little stories within stories.
我不知道该怎么形容，它们就是故事中的小故事。

264
00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:07.290
They're, they're, it's a Latsy, you know, from Commedia dell'arte, it's a Latsy and there's two amazing ones in this.
它们是……这是意大利即兴喜剧里的“拉齐”（Latsy），这剧里有两个非常棒的例子。

265
00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:10.210
And yeah, it was just a, just a pleasure to be a part of.
是的，能参与其中真是一种荣幸。

266
00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:11.250
No.
不。

267
00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.410
And it's, it's been so fun to rewatch.
重温这部剧真的很有趣。

268
00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:18.970
I think one of the things that keeps happening for me is I just appreciate you guys so much more.
我觉得我不断产生的一种感觉是，我比以前更加欣赏你们了。

269
00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:24.170
Like all the little nuances, all the choices people made, you just get to see it and sort of savor it.
就像那些细微的差别，每个人所做的选择，你都能看出来并细细品味。

270
00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:33.010
Yeah, I think getting distance from it and then rewatching it, you don't have any of the memories of what really happened when you were shooting it.
是啊，我觉得拉开距离再重温时，你已经没有了拍摄当时真实发生之事的记忆。

271
00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:37.530
So you're not attached to seeing a certain thing or a funny thing that you remember.
所以你不会执着于看到某个特定的东西，或者你记忆中好笑的片段。

272
00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:37.830
Yeah.
没错。

273
00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:41.030
You're looking at a moment in Amber in a very different way.
你正在以一种非常不同的方式审视这段被封存的时光。

274
00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:41.350
Yeah.
没错。

275
00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:47.470
You know, the Creed cold opening of manager and then tossing the keys to no one.
你知道，克里德那个经理身份的冷开场，然后把钥匙扔给空气。

276
00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:57.850
Like it just, it's a beautiful little comedic tip of the hat to like everything that Creed does best as a character and as an actor and performer.
这简直是对克里德作为角色、演员和表演者所擅长的一切，所致以的美妙喜剧敬意。

277
00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:03.230
And then they're writing to the actor's strengths and know exactly how to get the best laughs from Creed Bratton.
编剧们确实是在根据演员的强项来创作，他们非常清楚如何从克里德·布拉顿身上挖掘出最好的笑点。

278
00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:04.550
Yeah.
没错。

279
00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:09.950
We talked to Creed about his made up language and he said a little piece of backstory he had given himself,
我们和克里德聊过他自创的语言，他说他给自己设定了一小段背景故事，

280
00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:14.750
but he never told anyone is that he really thought maybe it would be revealed someday that Creed was an alien.
但他从未告诉过任何人，他真的觉得也许有一天会揭露克里德其实是个外星人。

281
00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.390
So he thought his made up language should sound like an alien language.
所以他觉得他自创的语言听起来应该像外星语言。

282
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.090
That is perfect.
那太完美了。

283
00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.730
That is perfect.
那太完美了。

284
00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.030
So it was intentional how he did it.
所以他那样做是有意为之的。

285
00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.230
I pitched, I rarely pitched episode ideas.
我曾提议过，虽然我很少提议剧集点子。

286
00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:32.430
I pitched a Creed episode that was 100% Creed and they didn't go for it.
我提议过一集完全关于克里德的剧集，但他们没采纳。

287
00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.470
It would have been way too experimental.
那会太实验性了。

288
00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:34.370
What was the premise?
前提是什么？

289
00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:43.170
The premise was they're just doing regular thing and there's Pam and Jim and it's the copy machine and something, you know, Michael comes in and blah, blah, blah.
前提是他们像往常一样做着日常工作，帕姆和吉姆在复印机旁，然后迈克尔进来了，诸如此类。

290
00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:49.550
And we think it's just a normal episode and then it kind of catches Creed and then Creed looks at the camera and he just gestures.
我们以为这只是普通的一集，然后镜头捕捉到了克里德，他看向镜头，做了一个手势。

291
00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.470
Come here.
过来。

292
00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:58.970
And he grabs his stuff and goes out the door and he keeps gesturing to the camera and gets the camera and puts it in his car.
他抓起东西走出门口，一直对着镜头招手，把摄像机带进他的车里。

293
00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.190
He's like, come with me.
他就像在说，跟我来。

294
00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:01.170
You need to see something.
你需要看点东西。

295
00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:05.970
And then we do 22 minute Odyssey into the life of Creed.
然后我们就进行了一场22分钟的克里德生活奥德赛。

296
00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:07.450
I would have loved that.
我一定会很喜欢那一集的。

297
00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:17.830
So it just goes like deep, like he's living in a warehouse and there's like dog fights down there and like he's got a whole other business that he's doing.
剧情会深入挖掘，比如他住在仓库里，下面有斗狗场，他还有另一套生意在运作。

298
00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:21.750
Like he takes to his home and they're like, daddy, and he's got all these children.
比如他回到家，孩子们喊他“爸爸”，他有这么多孩子。

299
00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:30.210
And like, you know, just like this, like all of the stuff that you are wondering about Creed and just like layers and layers of backstory.
你知道，就是那种你对克里德所有好奇的东西，一层又一层的背景故事。

300
00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.790
And the whole episode, I was like, there's no B story.
整集我都觉得，这集没有副线故事。

301
00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.690
It's just following Creed around.
就是跟着克里德到处转。

302
00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:40.230
You know, he goes into some ratty neighborhoods and maybe he's dealing drugs or whatever.
你知道，他会去一些破旧的街区，可能是在贩毒什么的。

303
00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:42.490
Like it gets just really weird.
就像是变得非常奇怪。

304
00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.010
And then he's Santa at the mall.
然后他又去商场扮圣诞老人。

305
00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:45.870
It's like, what?
简直让人摸不着头脑。

306
00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:46.250
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

307
00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.170
How do we end here?
我们怎么会落到这一步？

308
00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.810
And they were like, no.
他们当时说，不行。

309
00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:49.310
No.
不行。

310
00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.790
That could have been our whole season 10.
那本来可以成为我们第十季的全部内容。

311
00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:56.890
Just every episode, just follow someone out the door into their life.
每一集都跟着某个人走出大门，进入他们的生活。

312
00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:57.210
Yeah, into their life.
没错，进入他们的生活。

313
00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:57.890
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

314
00:12:58.330 --> 00:12:58.850
Fascinating.
太迷人了。

315
00:12:59.090 --> 00:12:59.210
Yeah.
是啊。

316
00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:02.510
Well, Rain, thank you for discussing The Office with us.
雷恩，谢谢你和我们讨论《办公室》。

317
00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.710
But you are also here to discuss something else.
但你今天来这里也是为了讨论别的事情。

318
00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.790
Your amazing book.
你那本了不起的书。

319
00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:06.930
Scrubs.
