所以你要清洗遗体，用亚麻布包裹，诵读祈祷文，并进行准备。

460
00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:27.530
But when you say you, you mean you personally, family members of the deceased.
但当你提到“你”的时候，指的是你自己，也就是逝者的家属。

461
00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:30.770
It doesn't have to be family members, but we really wanted to do it.
不一定非得是家属，但我们真的很想亲自去做。

462
00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.990
I wanted to be part of that, to experience that.
我想参与其中，去体验那个过程。

463
00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:40.310
And it's incredibly powerful to be, you know, frankly, washing the body of someone that, you
坦白说，清洗一个养育了你、你认识了79年的人的遗体，

464
00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:43.770
know, that raised you and that you've known for 79 years.
那种感觉是非常震撼的。

465
00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:47.670
But there was no bowl at the funeral home.
但殡仪馆里没有碗。

466
00:21:47.690 --> 00:21:48.990
You needed a bowl for water.
你需要一个碗来盛水。

467
00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:49.970
For water to wash.
用来清洗的水。

468
00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:55.330
And the guy was like, I've got a tea kettle you could use, or here's a styrofoam bowl to
那个人说，我有一个茶壶你可以用，或者这里有个泡沫塑料碗

469
00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.230
put the water in.
可以用来盛水。

470
00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:58.170
From like takeout food or something.
就像是外卖餐盒之类的东西。

471
00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:03.030
So it was in, and we were up against the wire because we were supposed to do this ritual
当时情况很紧急，我们时间紧迫，因为我们必须完成这个仪式，

472
00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:05.530
and then get over to the burial.
然后赶去安葬。

473
00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:07.510
And we had like 30 or 40 people coming.
而且我们还有大约30到40个人要来。

474
00:22:07.770 --> 00:22:09.510
So I ran to the target.
所以我跑去了塔吉特百货。

475
00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:13.790
It was in the middle of a heat wave looking for a bowl to have water in, an appropriate
当时正值热浪，我到处找一个碗来盛水，一个合适的

476
00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:16.410
bowl to wash my dead father's body.
用来清洗我父亲遗体的碗。

477
00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:19.710
So I use that as kind of a touch point for a conversation about death.
所以我把这个经历当作探讨死亡的一个切入点。

478
00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:25.210
And I also use the book as an opportunity to dig into some of life's biggest, most profound
我也利用这本书作为契机，去深入挖掘一些人生中最宏大、最深刻的问题，

479
00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:32.890
questions in what I hope is a fun, insightful, kind of goofy, upside down way, like death,
我希望以一种有趣、深刻、有点古怪、颠覆性的方式，比如死亡、

480
00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:37.770
consciousness, God, you know, the biggest questions of humanity.
意识、上帝，你知道的，人类最重大的问题。

481
00:22:38.010 --> 00:22:40.430
And I wanted to kind of put it through a Rainn Wilson lens.
我想通过雷恩·威尔森的视角来呈现这些内容。

482
00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:42.590
So that story was the way to get in.
所以那个故事就是切入点。

483
00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:43.730
It was fantastic.
太棒了。

484
00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:46.150
I shared part of that chapter with my daughter.
我和我女儿分享了那一章的部分内容。

485
00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:51.290
And in particular, Rainn, one thing I learned about you in this book that I didn't know is
特别是雷恩，我在书里了解到关于你的一件事，我之前并不知道，

486
00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:52.490
how much you love quotes.
那就是你有多么热爱名言警句。

487
00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:55.810
You quote a lot of amazing people in this book.
你在书里引用了许多了不起的人的话。

488
00:22:55.810 --> 00:23:00.190
And I was going to tell you one of the quotes I love that I always think of when I meet people
我正想告诉你一句我非常喜欢的名言，每当我见到别人时总会想起它，

489
00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:04.110
is it's from the chapter of Luke in the New Testament.
它出自《新约》中的路加福音那一章。

490
00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:05.930
It's part of a bigger verse.
它是更大一段经文的一部分。

491
00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:10.650
But the part that always sticks with me is the part that says, out of the abundance of the
但一直萦绕在我心头的那部分是，它说：心里所充满的，

492
00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:11.890
heart, the mouth speaks.
口里就说出来。

493
00:23:12.710 --> 00:23:18.090
And I think about that when I hear people talk, like what is their heart full of?
每当我听别人说话时，我都会想到这一点，他们的心里充满了什么？

494
00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:20.390
What are they sharing about?
他们在分享什么？

495
00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:22.190
What are they passionate about?
他们对什么充满热情？

496
00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:26.370
And it's just something that sticks with me throughout life.
这对我来说是一句终身受用的话。

497
00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:26.910
That's beautiful.
那太美了。

498
00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:29.090
I wish I would have used that in my book.
真希望我能在书里用上这句话。

499
00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:31.270
I wonder if I can fit it in the next edition.
不知道下一版能不能把它加进去。

500
00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:34.550
You know, I do want to say this is a very easy read.
你知道，我确实想说，这本书读起来非常轻松。

501
00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:37.650
I know we're talking about big, like heavy subjects.
我知道我们讨论的话题很宏大，很沉重。

502
00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:41.230
But you did write a book about big, heavy subjects.
但你确实写了一本关于宏大、沉重话题的书。

503
00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:42.430
And it's very entertaining.
而且它非常有趣。

504
00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:43.990
And it clips along.
读起来节奏明快。

505
00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:44.710
It is.
确实如此。

506
00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:45.410
It's funny.
它很幽默。

507
00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:46.070
It's relatable.
它很有共鸣。

508
00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:48.850
You hear your personality and your sense of humor.
你能从中听到你的个性和幽默感。

509
00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:52.150
And at the same time, you want to be a better person.
与此同时，它又让你想要成为一个更好的人。

510
00:23:52.150 --> 00:24:00.150
I particularly appreciated your section titled Yo Atheists and Why I'm Not an AtheiSt.
我特别欣赏你那篇题为《致无神论者：为什么我不是无神论者》的章节。

511
00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:07.410
And I really liked this because you are so interested in the arguments and beliefs of
我真的很喜欢这一点，因为你对那些与你截然不同的人的观点和信仰非常感兴趣。

512
00:24:07.410 --> 00:24:09.070
people who are very different from you.
与你截然不同的人。

513
00:24:09.070 --> 00:24:14.150
And you really show how to have a loving discourse with people who think differently.
你确实展示了如何与想法不同的人进行充满善意的交流。

514
00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:17.150
I loved your argument for why God exists.
我很喜欢你关于上帝为何存在的论点。

515
00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:20.350
But I also loved your respect for science.
但我也很喜欢你对科学的尊重。

516
00:24:21.210 --> 00:24:26.770
I just thought that is one of the things in the book where whatever your current faith is,
我只是觉得这是书中让我印象深刻的地方之一，无论你目前的信仰是什么，

517
00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:30.850
if you're a nunner, like you said, a lot of young people are checking the box,
如果你是“无宗教信仰者”，就像你说的，很多年轻人会勾选那一项，

518
00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:31.710
none of the above.
即“以上皆非”。

519
00:24:31.910 --> 00:24:37.950
Or if you are in an established faith or religion, this book respects you on every level,
或者如果你有既定的信仰或宗教，这本书在各个层面上都尊重你，

520
00:24:38.110 --> 00:24:39.370
even if you are an atheiSt.
即使你是个无神论者。

521
00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:41.430
It's the respect is there.
那种尊重是实实在在的。

522
00:24:41.430 --> 00:24:47.110
So, Rain, in Chapter 8, you say, hey, kids, let's build the perfect religion.
所以，Rain，在第八章里，你说，嘿，孩子们，让我们建立一个完美的宗教吧。

523
00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:50.450
The first sentence is, seriously, another chapter on religion?
第一句话就是，说真的，又是一个关于宗教的章节？

524
00:24:50.450 --> 00:24:51.590
You're killing me with this.
你真是要把我折磨死了。

525
00:24:53.870 --> 00:24:56.550
But at this point, you had explored so many.
但到了这一步，你已经探索了那么多种宗教。

526
00:24:56.590 --> 00:24:58.730
And you're like, what is the one that will bring us all together?
你就像是在问，哪一个能把我们所有人团结在一起呢？

527
00:24:59.390 --> 00:24:59.610
Yeah.
没错。

528
00:24:59.730 --> 00:25:05.150
And it was really great because you lay out all of the best parts of every religion,
这真的很棒，因为你列出了每个宗教中最精华的部分，

529
00:25:05.150 --> 00:25:06.450
the things they have in common.
也就是它们的共同点。

530
00:25:06.450 --> 00:25:10.990
And then you propose a new religion, which you call Soul Boom, TM.
然后你提出了一个新的宗教，你称之为“灵魂繁荣”（Soul Boom），商标。

531
00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:11.950
Trademark.
商标。

532
00:25:12.130 --> 00:25:12.530
Trademark.
商标。

533
00:25:12.770 --> 00:25:14.470
He actually typed that in the book, TM.
他真的在书里打出了“商标”这两个字。

534
00:25:15.130 --> 00:25:19.050
Now, it's very clear in the book that you aren't really starting a new religion.
现在，书中很明确地指出，你并不是真的要创立一个新宗教。

535
00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:19.950
Exactly.
没错。

536
00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:26.570
Rain, you were more just wanting to start a conversation about spirituality and just everyone's
Rain，你更多是想开启一场关于灵性以及每个人自己心路历程的对话。

537
00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:27.330
own journey.
每个人自己的旅程。

538
00:25:27.590 --> 00:25:30.950
Well, I do want to say I did really like the sound of this religion.
嗯，我想说我确实很喜欢这个宗教听起来的感觉。

539
00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:34.430
You mentioned it's very hard to get a new religion off the ground.
你提到创立一个新宗教非常困难。

540
00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:37.230
You need a religious leader, you know, all this kind of stuff.
你需要一位宗教领袖，你知道，诸如此类的东西。

541
00:25:37.490 --> 00:25:38.610
Yeah, which is not going to be me.
是啊，那个人肯定不会是我。

542
00:25:38.810 --> 00:25:39.070
Yeah.
没错。

543
00:25:39.270 --> 00:25:39.710
I know.
我知道。

544
00:25:39.830 --> 00:25:40.310
Maybe Creed.
也许可以是Creed。

545
00:25:41.110 --> 00:25:42.490
I have a pitch for you.
我有个提议给你。

546
00:25:42.570 --> 00:25:43.190
Okay, go ahead.
好，请说。

547
00:25:44.270 --> 00:25:44.670
Okay.
好的。

548
00:25:45.110 --> 00:25:48.350
When I was in college, I went to see a psychic.
我上大学的时候，去看过一次灵媒。

549
00:25:49.570 --> 00:25:54.230
And to be fair, I was asking if I was going to marry this boy that I had a crush on.
平心而论，我当时是在问我会不会嫁给那个我暗恋的男孩。

550
00:25:54.350 --> 00:25:54.470
Sure.
当然。

551
00:25:55.310 --> 00:25:56.470
That was my motivation.
那就是我的动力。

552
00:25:57.230 --> 00:25:58.510
The answer was no.
答案是否定的。

553
00:25:58.890 --> 00:25:59.230
Wow.
哇。

554
00:25:59.230 --> 00:26:00.310
He did not love me.
他不爱我。

555
00:26:00.470 --> 00:26:01.770
He was not going to marry me.
他根本没打算娶我。

556
00:26:02.070 --> 00:26:02.290
Okay.
好吧。

557
00:26:02.710 --> 00:26:03.490
Was it a woman?
是个女人吗？

558
00:26:03.650 --> 00:26:04.170
It was a woman.
是个女人。

559
00:26:04.250 --> 00:26:04.410
Okay.
好吧。

560
00:26:04.550 --> 00:26:05.510
How did she know?
她是怎么知道的？

561
00:26:05.690 --> 00:26:06.350
I mean.
我是说。

562
00:26:06.510 --> 00:26:07.150
What was the.
那到底是什么。

563
00:26:07.410 --> 00:26:09.270
I don't know, but she was right.
我不知道，但她说对了。

564
00:26:09.630 --> 00:26:10.270
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

565
00:26:10.330 --> 00:26:11.250
He didn't love me.
他不爱我。

566
00:26:11.490 --> 00:26:14.050
He loved three other girls at the same time as me.
他在跟我交往的同时还爱着另外三个女孩。

567
00:26:14.250 --> 00:26:14.970
He was one of those.
他就是那种人。

568
00:26:15.130 --> 00:26:15.430
Okay.
好吧。

569
00:26:15.650 --> 00:26:15.910
Okay.
好吧。

570
00:26:16.210 --> 00:26:17.890
So, whatever.
所以，无所谓了。

571
00:26:17.890 --> 00:26:19.150
She said, cut him loose.
她说，甩了他。

572
00:26:19.350 --> 00:26:20.390
It's not going to work out.
你们不会有结果的。

573
00:26:20.590 --> 00:26:20.850
Great.
太棒了。

574
00:26:20.990 --> 00:26:21.970
He loved Betsy Schnanzheiser.
他爱着贝琪·施南泽。

575
00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:23.870
He loved everybody else.
他爱着其他所有人。

576
00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:26.230
And Teresa von Villeneuve.
还有特蕾莎·冯·维伦纽夫。

577
00:26:26.250 --> 00:26:27.510
He had a lot of love in his heart.
他心里装满了爱。

578
00:26:27.650 --> 00:26:28.030
He did.
确实。

579
00:26:29.270 --> 00:26:30.230
And in his pants.
裤裆里也装满了。

580
00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:34.750
So, then I said, well, am I going to be successful in life?
然后我就问，我这辈子能成功吗？

581
00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:35.950
You know, I'm studying.
你知道的，我在读书。

582
00:26:36.150 --> 00:26:37.090
I'm a theater major.
我是戏剧专业的。

583
00:26:37.370 --> 00:26:38.830
I want to be a successful actress.
我想成为一名成功的演员。

584
00:26:39.050 --> 00:26:40.450
You're hitting her with the big questions.
你问的都是些大问题啊。

585
00:26:40.490 --> 00:26:40.930
I did.
我问了。

586
00:26:41.070 --> 00:26:41.810
I mean, you know.
我是说，你知道的。

587
00:26:41.990 --> 00:26:43.610
The only psychic I ever saw.
那是我唯一见过的一位灵媒。

588
00:26:44.050 --> 00:26:48.390
And she said, you're going to be very famous one day, but not for the reasons you think.
她说，你将来会很有名，但不是因为你以为的那些原因。

589
00:26:49.310 --> 00:26:55.270
She said, you're going to be famous in the area of religion.
她说，你会在宗教领域出名。

590
00:26:56.310 --> 00:26:58.910
You are going to be a famous religious leader.
你会成为一位著名的宗教领袖。

591
00:26:59.810 --> 00:27:00.370
Whoa.
哇。

592
00:27:01.770 --> 00:27:03.710
Do you want to run Soul Boom?
你想经营“灵魂繁荣”吗？

593
00:27:03.990 --> 00:27:05.190
That's what I'm saying.
我正想说这个。

594
00:27:05.190 --> 00:27:06.150
Is this your pitch?
这是你的推销词吗？

595
00:27:06.550 --> 00:27:07.070
Maybe.
也许吧。

596
00:27:07.370 --> 00:27:08.090
Soul Boom trademark.
“灵魂繁荣”商标。

597
00:27:08.390 --> 00:27:08.440
The religion.
那个宗教。

598
00:27:08.440 --> 00:27:09.410
It's all coming together.
一切都串联起来了。

599
00:27:09.850 --> 00:27:10.950
I love it.
我喜欢这个主意。

600
00:27:11.150 --> 00:27:12.870
I'm 100% behind that.
我百分之百支持你。

601
00:27:13.030 --> 00:27:13.730
Where do I start?
我该从哪儿开始呢？

602
00:27:13.730 --> 00:27:14.750
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

603
00:27:15.070 --> 00:27:16.450
You need another project.
你需要另一个项目。

604
00:27:17.090 --> 00:27:18.430
You're just saying to me.
你刚才是在跟我说。

605
00:27:18.670 --> 00:27:20.570
I want to take something really big on.
我想接手一个真正的大项目。

606
00:27:20.950 --> 00:27:21.130
Yeah.
是啊。

607
00:27:21.430 --> 00:27:21.650
Yeah.
没错。

608
00:27:21.890 --> 00:27:21.990
Yeah.
对。

609
00:27:22.210 --> 00:27:22.470
Perfect.
完美。

610
00:27:22.590 --> 00:27:23.310
What do I need to do?
我需要做什么？

611
00:27:23.410 --> 00:27:24.170
What do we need to do?
我们需要做什么？

612
00:27:24.330 --> 00:27:28.610
Well, we need to get you some kind of office or, you know.
嗯，我们需要给你弄个办公室之类的，或者你知道的。

613
00:27:28.990 --> 00:27:29.910
We're going to start with an office.
我们先从办公室开始。

614
00:27:29.910 --> 00:27:30.950
Worship center.
礼拜中心。

615
00:27:31.070 --> 00:27:31.870
Oh, an office.
哦，办公室。

616
00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:34.010
An outfit.
一套行头。

617
00:27:34.410 --> 00:27:37.250
You know, we need to get someone to design, you know.
你知道，我们需要找人来设计，你懂的。

618
00:27:37.410 --> 00:27:40.370
You mentioned in the book that you don't want, you know.
你在书里提到过你不想要，你知道的。

619
00:27:40.510 --> 00:27:40.970
No clergy.
不要神职人员。

620
00:27:41.170 --> 00:27:42.730
You don't want any clergy outfits.
你不想要任何神职人员的装束。

621
00:27:43.110 --> 00:27:43.390
That's true.
确实如此。

622
00:27:43.390 --> 00:27:44.570
You said no funny hats.
你说过不要滑稽的帽子。

623
00:27:44.570 --> 00:27:45.230
No funny hats.
不要滑稽的帽子。

624
00:27:45.290 --> 00:27:45.510
Yeah.
是啊。

625
00:27:45.970 --> 00:27:46.270
No.
不要。

626
00:27:46.730 --> 00:27:46.990
Yeah.
没错。

627
00:27:47.410 --> 00:27:47.830
I don't know.
我不知道。

628
00:27:47.970 --> 00:27:49.530
We'll put our heads together.
我们会一起商量一下。

629
00:27:49.710 --> 00:27:50.490
Let's figure this out.
我们来想办法解决。

630
00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:50.730
Okay.
好的。

631
00:27:50.730 --> 00:27:51.290
I love it.
我喜欢这个主意。

632
00:27:51.410 --> 00:27:52.730
Well, I don't know.
嗯，我不知道。

633
00:27:52.790 --> 00:27:55.250
Maybe we'll make this woman's prediction come true.
也许我们会让这个女人的预言成真。

634
00:27:55.330 --> 00:27:59.010
I did say that one of the components of the building a perfect religion is no clergy.
我确实说过建立完美宗教的要素之一就是没有神职人员。

635
00:27:59.010 --> 00:28:01.190
But I'm willing to reverse that.
但我愿意推翻这一点。

636
00:28:01.630 --> 00:28:01.890
Really?
真的吗？

637
00:28:02.170 --> 00:28:02.310
Yeah.
是的。

638
00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:04.010
This was a very quick reversal.
这反转得也太快了。

639
00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:04.430
Yeah.
是啊。

640
00:28:04.430 --> 00:28:06.570
That felt like an important tenet of your religion.
那感觉像是你宗教中很重要的一条教义。

641
00:28:06.570 --> 00:28:07.890
And you are backtracking quickly.
而你现在却迅速反悔了。

642
00:28:08.150 --> 00:28:09.930
I feel like there's like five people that could do it.
我觉得大概只有五个人能胜任。

643
00:28:10.010 --> 00:28:11.050
Like you and Oprah.
比如你和奥普拉。

644
00:28:11.330 --> 00:28:13.170
And I don't even know who else.
我甚至不知道还有谁。

645
00:28:14.030 --> 00:28:14.910
Maybe Creed.
也许克里德可以。

646
00:28:15.330 --> 00:28:15.610
Yeah.
没错。

647
00:28:15.870 --> 00:28:16.070
Wow.
哇。

648
00:28:16.210 --> 00:28:17.090
Creed could run security.
克里德可以负责安保。

649
00:28:19.350 --> 00:28:20.350
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

650
00:28:20.510 --> 00:28:22.010
Guys, please read the book.
伙计们，请读读这本书。

651
00:28:22.170 --> 00:28:26.790
And let us know if you think I should start the Soul Boom religion.
如果你觉得我应该创立“灵魂繁荣”教，请告诉我们。

652
00:28:29.010 --> 00:28:30.870
Well, Rain, thank you for coming in today.
好的，雷恩，谢谢你今天能来。

653
00:28:31.110 --> 00:28:32.830
We also want to mention one other thing.
我们还要提另一件事。

654
00:28:32.930 --> 00:28:36.450
So Soul Boom, Why We Need a Spiritual Revolution on sale now.
《灵魂繁荣：为什么我们需要一场精神革命》现已发售。

655
00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:36.850
Yep.
没错。

656
00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:40.630
And then in May, you've got a show coming out on Peacock.
五月份你还有一档节目要在Peacock上线。

657
00:28:40.930 --> 00:28:42.050
May 20th.
5月20日。

658
00:28:42.170 --> 00:28:42.610
That's right.
没错。

659
00:28:42.970 --> 00:28:44.090
The Geography of Bliss.
《幸福地理学》。

660
00:28:44.390 --> 00:28:45.750
Talk about dream jobs.
这简直是梦想工作。

661
00:28:45.970 --> 00:28:47.910
I flew around the world looking for happiness.
我飞遍全球去寻找幸福。

662
00:28:47.910 --> 00:28:53.930
How can we find clues to happiness, fulfillment, meaning, joy from other cultures around the
我们如何从世界各地的其他文化中找到关于幸福、满足、意义和快乐的线索呢？

663
00:28:53.930 --> 00:28:54.070
world?
世界？

664
00:28:54.190 --> 00:28:58.390
We got to go to Iceland, Thailand, Ghana, West Africa, Bulgaria.
我们去了冰岛、泰国、西非的加纳和保加利亚。

665
00:28:58.950 --> 00:29:02.250
And we did an episode right here in Los Angeles as well.
我们还在洛杉矶拍了一集。

666
00:29:02.570 --> 00:29:04.050
Super fun and interesting.
超级有趣，非常有意思。

667
00:29:04.450 --> 00:29:09.430
And I call it like it's Anthony Bourdain, but instead of food, it's joy.
我把它称为安东尼·波登式的节目，只不过主题不是美食，而是快乐。

668
00:29:10.030 --> 00:29:12.350
Oh, I can't wait to watch it.
噢，我迫不及待想看了。

669
00:29:12.430 --> 00:29:13.230
Yeah, it's a lot of fun.
是的，非常有趣。

670
00:29:13.370 --> 00:29:14.450
It's quirky.
它很古怪。

671
00:29:14.450 --> 00:29:15.090
It's funny.
它很搞笑。

672
00:29:15.090 --> 00:29:17.670
But it also gets a little profound here and there.
但偶尔也会变得深刻。

673
00:29:18.010 --> 00:29:18.650
That is you, Rain.
那确实是你，雷恩。

674
00:29:18.650 --> 00:29:19.390
That sounds like you.
听起来很像你。

675
00:29:19.650 --> 00:29:19.770
Yeah.
是啊。

676
00:29:20.510 --> 00:29:20.990
Maybe.
也许吧。

677
00:29:21.550 --> 00:29:24.090
Well, you guys, check out Rain's new book, Soul Boom.
好了，各位，去看看雷恩的新书《灵魂繁荣》吧。

678
00:29:24.310 --> 00:29:25.670
And we just love you so much.
我们真的非常爱你。

679
00:29:25.770 --> 00:29:27.010
Thanks for being here today, Rain.
谢谢你今天能来，雷恩。

680
00:29:27.010 --> 00:29:28.270
I love you, Office Ladies.
我也爱你们，《办公室女士》。

681
00:29:28.470 --> 00:29:29.830
Thanks for having me on your show.
谢谢你们邀请我上节目。

682
00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:34.270
We'll be back to break down the rest of Search Committee Part 2.
我们稍后回来继续解析《搜寻委员会》第二部分。

683
00:29:34.970 --> 00:29:49.020
It's time to break down the rest of this episode, Search Party Part 2.
是时候继续解析这一集《搜寻委员会》第二部分了。

684
00:29:49.280 --> 00:29:49.960
Search Committee.
《搜寻委员会》。

685
00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:51.200
Thank you.
谢谢。

686
00:29:51.380 --> 00:29:52.100
Search Committee.
《搜寻委员会》。

687
00:29:52.640 --> 00:29:54.320
Good to know what episode we're doing.
知道我们在讲哪一集真好。

688
00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:55.860
Off to a good start.
开了个好头。

689
00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:56.540
All right.
好的。

690
00:29:56.540 --> 00:30:04.180
Well, Joe is going to enter with a new set of dogs, actually sort of one of each dog now.
乔带着一群新狗进来了，实际上现在每种狗都有一只。

691
00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:05.020
Yeah.
没错。

692
00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:11.440
She hands off her bags and her dogs to Gabe, and she starts chatting with Jim about this
她把包和狗交给盖博，然后开始和吉姆聊起今天早上的《霍华德·斯特恩秀》。

693
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:12.880
morning's episode of Howard Stern.
你知道，他很棒，但她觉得真正出彩的是罗宾。

694
00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:16.560
You know, he's great, but really, she feels like it's Robin.
罗宾才是亮点，对吧？

695
00:30:17.340 --> 00:30:18.780
Robin is the highlight, right?
但那是霍华德的节目。

696
00:30:18.900 --> 00:30:20.040
But it's Howard's show.
嗯哼。

697
00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:20.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

698
00:30:20.640 --> 00:30:20.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

699
00:30:21.040 --> 00:30:23.520
I love when Joe makes small talk.
我喜欢乔闲聊的时候。

700
00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:28.640
You never know what it's going to be about, and I'm fascinated by her and her life.
你永远不知道她会聊什么，我对她和她的生活着迷不已。

701
00:30:29.080 --> 00:30:30.880
For me, the spinoff would have been Joe.
对我来说，衍生剧的主角应该是乔。

702
00:30:31.960 --> 00:30:32.320
Yeah.
没错。

703
00:30:32.720 --> 00:30:32.980
Where is Joe?
乔去哪了？

704
00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:34.120
But Joe's personal life.
我是说乔的私生活。

705
00:30:34.200 --> 00:30:35.360
I don't need to see her at work.
我不想看她在工作时的样子。

706
00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:35.660
No.
不想。

707
00:30:35.660 --> 00:30:37.400
Only when she comes to Dunder Mifflin.
只看她来邓德·米夫林公司的时候就行。

708
00:30:38.020 --> 00:30:38.380
Okay.
好吧。

709
00:30:38.620 --> 00:30:38.740
All right.
行吧。

710
00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:39.860
You know, like, we're a side note.
你知道，我们就像是配角一样。

711
00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:41.620
What is she doing outside of work?
她在工作之外都在做什么？

712
00:30:41.760 --> 00:30:41.960
Yeah.
是啊。

713
00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:43.140
That's the show I want to see.
那才是我真正想看的剧。

714
00:30:43.340 --> 00:30:43.560
In Florida.
在佛罗里达。

715
00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:44.200
Yeah.
没错。

716
00:30:44.740 --> 00:30:49.020
Well, she's going to notice Daryl's resume is on the top of the pile, and she's really happy
嗯，她会注意到达里尔的简历放在最上面，她很高兴

717
00:30:49.020 --> 00:30:51.400
to see, you know, someone she knows.
能看到一个她认识的人。

718
00:30:51.540 --> 00:30:51.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

719
00:30:52.260 --> 00:30:53.200
Someone in-house.
一个公司内部的人。

720
00:30:53.380 --> 00:30:54.900
But why is it four pages long?
但为什么简历有四页那么长？

721
00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:59.320
Yeah, and she reads part of his resume, and she looks at him and says, you coordinated
是啊，她读了一部分简历，然后看着他说，你协调

722
00:30:59.320 --> 00:31:05.520
and implemented receipt, storage, and delivery of over 2.5 billion units of inventory?
并执行了超过25亿单位库存的接收、存储和交付？

723
00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:07.820
2.5 billion, Daryl?
25亿，达里尔？

724
00:31:08.040 --> 00:31:10.580
2.5 billion units of what?
25亿单位的什么？

725
00:31:11.020 --> 00:31:13.140
And Daryl says, paper material?
达里尔说，纸质材料？

726
00:31:13.600 --> 00:31:15.020
Like pieces of paper.
就像纸片一样。

727
00:31:15.220 --> 00:31:15.380
Yeah.
是啊。

728
00:31:16.540 --> 00:31:17.980
Lady, I was curious.
大姐，我当时只是好奇。

729
00:31:18.460 --> 00:31:19.520
About paper?
对纸好奇？

730
00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:20.120
No.
不是。

731
00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:24.980
About resumes, and how often do we lie on our resumes?
是对简历好奇，我们到底在简历上撒过多少次谎？

732
00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:27.360
Have you ever lied on a resume?
你在简历上撒过谎吗？

733
00:31:28.080 --> 00:31:33.500
No, but I have definitely added a flourish in special skills, as we've talked about.
没有，但我确实在特长一栏里润色过，我们之前聊过这个。

734
00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:33.860
Yeah.
是啊。

735
00:31:33.860 --> 00:31:38.000
You know, I mean, I wouldn't normally put water skiing, but I have.
你知道，我平时不会写滑水，但我写过。

736
00:31:38.240 --> 00:31:41.460
I don't think anyone thinks what I can do on a water ski is special.
我觉得没人会觉得我的滑水技术有什么特别的。

737
00:31:44.100 --> 00:31:44.620
Okay.
好吧。

738
00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:50.300
This led me to an article on CNBC.com from December of 2022.
这让我找到了一篇2022年12月CNBC网站上的文章。

739
00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:57.300
It said, over 55% of people admit to lying on their resume at least once.
文章说，超过55%的人承认至少在简历上撒过一次谎。

740
00:31:57.900 --> 00:32:03.940
And according to the survey done by Standout CV, they surveyed Americans 18 years and older,
根据Standout CV的一项调查，他们调查了18岁及以上的美国人，

741
00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:06.180
and this is what they found out.
这就是他们的发现。

742
00:32:06.920 --> 00:32:12.400
The number of Google searches about how to fake a resume was up 48%.
关于如何伪造简历的谷歌搜索量上升了48%。

743
00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:13.020
What?
什么？

744
00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:20.020
In 2022, specifically related to faking a job reference was up 52%.
在2022年，专门关于伪造工作推荐信的搜索量上升了52%。

745
00:32:20.020 --> 00:32:21.840
You can Google that?
这也能谷歌搜到？

746
00:32:22.360 --> 00:32:24.860
Y'all were Googling how to fake your resume.
你们居然都在谷歌上搜怎么伪造简历。

747
00:32:26.340 --> 00:32:28.540
So, this led me to this.
所以，这引出了这个话题。

748
00:32:28.700 --> 00:32:30.320
What were people lying about?
人们都在哪些方面撒谎？

749
00:32:30.700 --> 00:32:35.260
Here are the eight most common resume lies, according to Standout CV.
根据Standout CV的调查，以下是简历中最常见的八个谎言。

750
00:32:35.260 --> 00:32:36.080
Okay.
好的。

751
00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:38.700
Previous work experience.
过往工作经验。

752
00:32:39.120 --> 00:32:40.620
Just making stuff up?
只是在编造吗？

753
00:32:40.700 --> 00:32:40.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

754
00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:43.340
55% of people lie about that.
55%的人会在这上面撒谎。

755
00:32:43.760 --> 00:32:44.060
Wow.
哇。

756
00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:44.920
Skills.
技能。

757
00:32:45.340 --> 00:32:46.920
That seems like it's important.
这看起来很重要。

758
00:32:47.560 --> 00:32:50.460
43% of people lie about that.
43%的人会在这上面撒谎。

759
00:32:51.040 --> 00:32:54.180
College degree are equivalent.
大学学位及同等学历。

760
00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:55.960
41%.
41%。

761
00:32:55.960 --> 00:32:56.900
Why?
为什么？

762
00:32:57.440 --> 00:33:00.220
I mean, aren't people going to, like, follow up on that?
我是说，难道人们不会去核实这些吗？

763
00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:01.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

764
00:33:02.140 --> 00:33:02.860
I guess not.
我想不会吧。

765
00:33:02.860 --> 00:33:06.620
But personal details, location, name, et cetera.
但个人信息、住址、姓名之类的。

766
00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:08.580
Age, 39%.
年龄，39%。

767
00:33:08.580 --> 00:33:09.800
Lie about that.
在这上面撒谎。

768
00:33:10.100 --> 00:33:10.260
Okay.
好吧。

769
00:33:10.900 --> 00:33:13.280
High school details, 39% lie.
高中经历，39%的人撒谎。

770
00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:14.880
Previous salary.
过往薪资。

771
00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:15.500
Ooh.
噢。

772
00:33:16.020 --> 00:33:18.060
33% lie about that.
33%的人会在这上面撒谎。

773
00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:22.320
I just want to say, if you're going to lie about anything, pad that previous salary.
我只想说，如果你非要撒谎，就把过往薪资往高了报。

774
00:33:22.320 --> 00:33:22.840
Exactly.
没错。

775
00:33:22.940 --> 00:33:25.720
What are you messing with all the other stuff for?
你干嘛要在其他事情上动歪脑筋呢？

776
00:33:26.080 --> 00:33:27.260
You heard it here.
你们都听到了。

777
00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:28.900
Lie about your previous salary.
在过往薪资上撒谎吧。

778
00:33:29.120 --> 00:33:29.300
Yes.
是的。

779
00:33:29.900 --> 00:33:32.820
Job-specific software are equipment skills.
特定工作的软件或设备技能。

780
00:33:33.020 --> 00:33:33.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

781
00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:35.560
33% lie about that.
33%的人会在这上面撒谎。

782
00:33:35.980 --> 00:33:36.140
Yeah.
是啊。

783
00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:36.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

784
00:33:37.300 --> 00:33:41.980
Last on what people lie about, employer references, 21%.
最后是人们撒谎的内容，雇主推荐信，21%。

785
00:33:42.780 --> 00:33:45.080
That seems like you're going to get caught.
这看起来很容易被拆穿。

786
00:33:45.240 --> 00:33:45.840
I know.
我知道。

787
00:33:46.200 --> 00:33:50.960
This led me to the question, what professions are lied about the most?
这让我产生了一个疑问，哪些职业的人最爱撒谎？

788
00:33:51.180 --> 00:33:51.700
Oh.
噢。

789
00:33:51.960 --> 00:33:53.380
When applying for these jobs.
在申请这些工作时。

790
00:33:53.860 --> 00:33:58.460
The industry with the most employees lying on their resumes is manufacturing.
简历造假员工最多的行业是制造业。

791
00:33:59.420 --> 00:34:03.040
With 72% of employees straying from the truth.
有72%的员工不诚实。

792
00:34:03.340 --> 00:34:08.360
The survey also found the next industry that had the most people lying on their resumes
调查还发现，简历造假人数排名第二的行业

793
00:34:08.360 --> 00:34:10.760
was the healthcare industry.
是医疗保健行业。

794
00:34:11.720 --> 00:34:12.800
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

795
00:34:13.360 --> 00:34:14.000
64%.
64%。

796
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:18.860
And then the third most lied about profession was the arts.
第三个简历造假最多的行业是艺术行业。

797
00:34:19.340 --> 00:34:19.980
Oh.
噢。

798
00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:21.540
At 63%.
占比63%。

799
00:34:21.540 --> 00:34:23.200
Water skiing, special skills.
滑水，特殊技能。

800
00:34:23.300 --> 00:34:23.940
Yeah, exactly.
是啊，没错。

801
00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:24.260
Me.
我。

802
00:34:24.580 --> 00:34:25.180
Be me.
