就因为这些引人入胜的情节线。

967
00:40:20.040 --> 00:40:20.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

968
00:40:20.740 --> 00:40:21.180
All right.
好的。

969
00:40:21.880 --> 00:40:26.820
Next up is the scene where Aaron is going to bring in Mr. Jacques Souvenir, the Frenchman.
接下来是亚伦带雅克·苏文尼先生，那个法国人进来的场景。

970
00:40:26.940 --> 00:40:28.840
We talked with Rain about this scene.
我们和雷恩讨论过这个场景。

971
00:40:28.960 --> 00:40:29.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

972
00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:32.920
I guess all I have to say now here in the breakdown is that I love it.
我想我现在在剧本分析里唯一要说的就是，我太喜欢这个了。

973
00:40:33.280 --> 00:40:35.400
I'm pretty sure his name was Jacques Souvenir.
我挺确定他叫雅克·苏文尼。

974
00:40:35.900 --> 00:40:36.900
Oh, I'm so sorry.
噢，真抱歉。

975
00:40:37.040 --> 00:40:38.460
You said it the way Joe says it.
你刚才说的语调跟乔一模一样。

976
00:40:38.700 --> 00:40:38.980
Yes.
是的。

977
00:40:39.180 --> 00:40:39.940
So sorry.
非常抱歉。

978
00:40:40.360 --> 00:40:40.940
You're right.
你说得对。

979
00:40:41.120 --> 00:40:41.840
He is French.
他是法国人。

980
00:40:42.580 --> 00:40:47.700
After Dwight leaves the conference room, Joe's like, all right, who are the real contenders?
德怀特离开会议室后，乔就问，好吧，谁才是真正的竞争者？

981
00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:48.560
What about Andy?
安迪怎么样？

982
00:40:48.820 --> 00:40:50.440
And Gabe just goes off.
然后盖博就爆发了。

983
00:40:50.560 --> 00:40:51.540
And she's like, you know what, Gabe?
她说，你知道吗，盖博？

984
00:40:51.960 --> 00:40:53.720
I think it's time to get you back to Florida.
我觉得是时候送你回佛罗里达了。

985
00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:55.540
You got too close to the people here.
你和这里的人走得太近了。

986
00:40:55.740 --> 00:40:56.640
We need to get you home.
我们需要送你回家。

987
00:40:56.820 --> 00:41:00.980
Well, this is a big plot point because it means we're going to say goodbye to Gabe for a little while.
嗯，这是一个重要的情节转折，因为这意味着我们要暂时和盖博告别了。

988
00:41:00.980 --> 00:41:06.920
Well, Gabe is going to be back in season eight, and this is reminding me we need to reach out to Zach Woods and have him on this podcaSt.
嗯，盖博在第八季会回来，这提醒我我们需要联系扎克·伍兹，邀请他来上我们的播客。

989
00:41:07.180 --> 00:41:07.660
I know.
我知道。

990
00:41:07.920 --> 00:41:09.460
I have a lot I need to speak with him about.
我有很多话想跟他聊。

991
00:41:09.460 --> 00:41:11.240
Zach, I just want to hang out with you.
扎克，我只是想和你聚聚。

992
00:41:12.800 --> 00:41:14.740
That's kind of what this podcast is for.
这大概就是这个播客的初衷吧。

993
00:41:14.880 --> 00:41:15.020
Yeah.
是啊。

994
00:41:15.640 --> 00:41:21.560
Well, Jim is going to walk Joe to her car, and she asked him, how did her friend Nellie do in the interview?
吉姆送乔去车上，她问吉姆，她的朋友奈莉面试表现如何？

995
00:41:22.460 --> 00:41:25.280
Jim said, well, we didn't know that Nellie was your friend.
吉姆说，嗯，我们不知道奈莉是你的朋友。

996
00:41:25.540 --> 00:41:28.800
And Joe is like, that's a kind of classy move, right?
乔就说，这招挺高明的，对吧？

997
00:41:29.540 --> 00:41:32.060
But Jim's like, you know, we still don't think she's a good fit.
但吉姆说，你知道，我们还是觉得她不太合适。

998
00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:34.980
And then this is a surprise moment.
然后这是一个令人惊讶的时刻。

999
00:41:36.360 --> 00:41:39.020
Joe tells Jim, go ahead and give Dwight an interview.
乔告诉吉姆，去给德怀特一个面试机会吧。

1000
00:41:39.580 --> 00:41:40.900
I like a little crazy.
我就喜欢带点疯狂劲儿的。

1001
00:41:41.700 --> 00:41:44.800
I can't believe she's going to give him another interview after everything.
真不敢相信，发生了这么多事，她竟然还要再采访他一次。

1002
00:41:45.080 --> 00:41:46.360
And then her trunk opens.
然后她的后备箱打开了。

1003
00:41:46.520 --> 00:41:48.940
Did you see how it opens onto Jim?
你看到它打开时正好对着吉姆了吗？

1004
00:41:49.080 --> 00:41:51.260
Yeah, and he like bends out of the way.
看到了，他就像是弯腰躲开了。

1005
00:41:52.160 --> 00:41:56.820
Up next is one of my favorite Oscar moments for the whole entire season seven.
接下来是第七季中我最喜欢的奥斯卡时刻之一。

1006
00:41:57.020 --> 00:41:57.840
What is it?
是什么？

1007
00:41:57.840 --> 00:42:02.520
It is just one of those tiny throwaway moments, but it made me laugh so hard.
那只是一个微不足道的小插曲，但我当时笑得特别厉害。

1008
00:42:02.620 --> 00:42:04.860
I rewound the scene and watched it again.
我把那一幕倒回去又看了一遍。

1009
00:42:05.580 --> 00:42:08.540
Oscar's going to walk up to front reception to drop off a package.
奥斯卡走到前台去送一个包裹。

1010
00:42:09.040 --> 00:42:12.400
A gray sock puppet with a red bow greets him.
一个系着红蝴蝶结的灰色袜子木偶向他打招呼。

1011
00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:15.400
Oscar says, Aaron, what are you doing?
奥斯卡说：“亚伦，你在干什么？”

1012
00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:18.180
Aaron says, I've been turned into a puppet.
亚伦说：“我变成了一个木偶。”

1013
00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:20.400
And Oscar goes, okay.
奥斯卡回了句：“好吧。”

1014
00:42:21.840 --> 00:42:23.800
And just walks away.
然后就直接走开了。

1015
00:42:24.240 --> 00:42:26.360
Doesn't entertain the puppet.
完全没理会那个木偶。

1016
00:42:26.540 --> 00:42:28.280
Doesn't stay around to find out why.
也没留下来问个究竟。

1017
00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:29.280
He's like, no, okay.
他就像是说，不，好吧。

1018
00:42:29.640 --> 00:42:31.040
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢这一幕了。

1019
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.520
We got a fan question from Kristen S.
我们收到了一位粉丝克里斯汀·S的提问。

1020
00:42:33.660 --> 00:42:35.200
In New Brunswick, Canada, who said,
她来自加拿大新不伦瑞克省，她说：

1021
00:42:35.300 --> 00:42:41.460
Kevin's talking head about the puppets is what I believe to be the most underrated comedy bit in the office.
凯文关于木偶的采访片段，我认为是《办公室》里最被低估的喜剧桥段。

1022
00:42:41.460 --> 00:42:43.680
I laugh out loud every time.
我每次看都忍不住大笑。

1023
00:42:43.900 --> 00:42:47.120
My son plays it for me just to hear me laugh.
我儿子专门放给我看，就是为了听我笑。

1024
00:42:47.680 --> 00:42:50.560
Brian Baumgartner's earnest delivery is perfection.
布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳那本正经的演绎简直完美。

1025
00:42:51.060 --> 00:42:53.680
Well, Kristen, I totally agreed with you.
嗯，克里斯汀，我完全同意你的看法。

1026
00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:55.860
And I felt like we should hear this talking head.
我觉得我们应该重温一下这个采访片段。

1027
00:42:56.760 --> 00:43:00.360
It's just that I wish the puppets would talk more about the alphabet.
我只是希望木偶们能多讲讲字母表。

1028
00:43:01.080 --> 00:43:08.460
Not for me, but if any kids are watching, A, B, and so forth.
不是为了我，但如果有孩子在看的话，A、B之类的。

1029
00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:16.520
You know, M-N-L-O, P, F.
你知道的，M-N-L-O，P，F。

1030
00:43:17.940 --> 00:43:24.600
Yes, this is the moment we find out that Kevin thinks M-N-L-O is a letter in the alphabet,
没错，这一刻我们发现凯文认为M-N-L-O是字母表里的字母，

1031
00:43:24.600 --> 00:43:26.100
which brought me to this, Jenna.
这让我想到了这一点，珍娜。

1032
00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:28.500
His last name is Malone.
他的姓是马龙（Malone）。

1033
00:43:28.780 --> 00:43:33.440
He has an M, he has an L, an O, and an N in his name.
他的名字里有M、L、O和N。

1034
00:43:34.060 --> 00:43:35.800
Can he spell his name?
他会拼自己的名字吗？

1035
00:43:36.540 --> 00:43:38.620
It doesn't seem like it.
看起来好像不会。

1036
00:43:39.360 --> 00:43:40.500
Perhaps not.
或许吧。

1037
00:43:41.360 --> 00:43:48.160
Well, the hand puppet is going to explain that she needs a date with the best salesman in the office, Andy Bernard.
嗯，那个手偶要解释说她想和办公室里最棒的销售员安迪·伯纳德约会。

1038
00:43:48.720 --> 00:43:53.660
Yeah, Andy walks over and he says he's flattered,
对，安迪走过去说他很受宠若惊，

1039
00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:56.580
but he doesn't think that they should date.
但他觉得他们不应该约会。

1040
00:43:57.300 --> 00:43:57.700
Ouch.
哎哟。

1041
00:43:58.700 --> 00:44:01.440
Oh, I mean, I would just have to, that would be it.
噢，我的意思是，如果是我，那肯定就完了。

1042
00:44:01.540 --> 00:44:02.280
I would leave.
我会直接走人。

1043
00:44:02.500 --> 00:44:03.340
I'm done working here.
我不干了。

1044
00:44:03.620 --> 00:44:04.360
Bye, everybody.
大家再见。

1045
00:44:04.840 --> 00:44:06.000
That's so embarrassing.
那太尴尬了。

1046
00:44:06.360 --> 00:44:07.880
I would not be able to come back from that.
我肯定没法面对这种局面。

1047
00:44:07.880 --> 00:44:14.240
He has a talking head that is really a series of talking heads, I guess, right?
他有一个采访片段，其实是一系列采访片段，对吧？

1048
00:44:14.440 --> 00:44:22.700
He gives a lot of reasons for why he doesn't think they should date, that, you know, Aaron's his best friend, but he just didn't feel it.
他给出了很多理由解释为什么觉得他们不该约会，你知道的，比如亚伦是他最好的朋友，但他就是没那种感觉。

1049
00:44:22.800 --> 00:44:30.780
Or he's got a really weird thing about how, like, sometimes you really want to like things, but you just can't seem to, like Mad Men or football.
或者他有一种很奇怪的想法，就是有时候你真的很想喜欢某些东西，但就是喜欢不起来，比如《广告狂人》或者橄榄球。

1050
00:44:31.380 --> 00:44:34.580
And then he sort of says, like, maybe he got over Aaron.
然后他大概说了句，也许他已经放下亚伦了。

1051
00:44:34.780 --> 00:44:36.040
There's, like, so many reasons.
怎么说呢，原因实在太多了。

1052
00:44:36.380 --> 00:44:39.160
Well, he also said, let's not forget she chose Gabe over me.
嗯，他还说，别忘了她选了盖博没选我。

1053
00:44:39.640 --> 00:44:40.580
That one hurt.
那句话挺伤人的。

1054
00:44:41.060 --> 00:44:43.660
But then he ends with, well, actually, she's pretty great.
但他最后又补了一句，其实，她真的很不错。

1055
00:44:44.440 --> 00:44:45.400
I'm confused.
我糊涂了。

1056
00:44:45.740 --> 00:44:46.860
I think he is, too.
我想他自己也糊涂着呢。

1057
00:44:47.520 --> 00:44:50.820
Next up, we get to meet the new bridezilla in the office.
接下来，我们要见识一下办公室里新晋的“新娘怪兽”。

1058
00:44:51.380 --> 00:44:53.060
I really loved doing this scene.
我真的很喜欢拍这场戏。

1059
00:44:53.940 --> 00:44:56.360
Angela has only been engaged a few hours.
安吉拉订婚才不过几个小时。

1060
00:44:56.360 --> 00:45:03.380
You guys, like a few hours, like three hours, and she's already making big plans and telling people they're not going to be invited.
伙计们，才几个小时，也就三个小时吧，她就开始做各种宏大的计划，还告诉别人他们没份参加。

1061
00:45:03.580 --> 00:45:08.560
She's like, Stanley, I won't be able to invite everyone to the wedding because we want to keep it to $3.50.
她对斯坦利说，我没法邀请所有人参加婚礼，因为我们想把预算控制在3.5美元以内。

1062
00:45:09.360 --> 00:45:11.100
Stanley's like, I'll get over it.
斯坦利回她，我会挺过来的。

1063
00:45:12.860 --> 00:45:20.640
Angela's like, I mean, we just have to see how many senators and members of Congress want to attend before we can open it up, you know, to regular people.
安吉拉又说，我的意思是，我们得先看看有多少参议员和国会议员想来，才能决定要不要邀请普通人。

1064
00:45:20.640 --> 00:45:26.480
And then she says, Pam, you know how you and Jim did your ironic wedding?
然后她说，帕姆，你记得你和吉姆办的那场反讽式婚礼吗？

1065
00:45:26.780 --> 00:45:29.820
Do you still have the plans for the dream wedding that you couldn't afford?
你们还有那场你们办不起的梦幻婚礼的计划书吗？

1066
00:45:30.320 --> 00:45:33.360
And Pam says, that was our dream wedding.
帕姆说，那场就是我们的梦幻婚礼。

1067
00:45:33.900 --> 00:45:37.120
And Angela says, Niagara Falls?
安吉拉说，尼亚加拉大瀑布？

1068
00:45:38.160 --> 00:45:38.700
Pregnant?
怀孕了？

1069
00:45:39.360 --> 00:45:40.720
That was your dream?
那就是你们的梦想？

1070
00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:42.640
Pork medallions?
猪肉奖章？

1071
00:45:43.900 --> 00:45:45.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1072
00:45:45.420 --> 00:45:47.580
She is going to be horrible to deal with.
跟她打交道肯定会很痛苦。

1073
00:45:47.900 --> 00:45:49.680
Pam gives a little look to Oscar.
帕姆看了奥斯卡一眼。

1074
00:45:51.180 --> 00:45:53.040
And he gives her a look back like, Pam.
奥斯卡回了她一个眼神，好像在说，帕姆啊。

1075
00:45:53.200 --> 00:45:55.100
And then she goes, very weighted.
然后她开口了，语气非常沉重。

1076
00:45:55.340 --> 00:45:59.540
She says, Angela, I hope you have a very beautiful wedding.
她说，安吉拉，我希望你能拥有一场非常美丽的婚礼。

1077
00:46:01.360 --> 00:46:03.100
That ain't what she really means.
她心里可不是这么想的。

1078
00:46:03.640 --> 00:46:07.520
Well, let's take a break because when we come back, Kelly has joined the search committee.
好了，我们先休息一下，回来后凯莉会加入搜寻委员会。

1079
00:46:07.700 --> 00:46:10.020
And things are going to get a little dicey.
事情会变得有点棘手。

1080
00:46:19.760 --> 00:46:20.860
We're back from break.
我们休息回来了。

1081
00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:25.380
And before we keep breaking down this episode, Angela, I have something for you.
在继续拆解这一集之前，安吉拉，我有个东西要给你。

1082
00:46:25.700 --> 00:46:26.140
What?
什么？

1083
00:46:26.600 --> 00:46:30.900
You know, we haven't had a chance to talk about our live show in Vancouver that we did.
你知道，我们还没机会聊聊我们在温哥华办的那场现场秀。

1084
00:46:31.040 --> 00:46:32.700
We haven't talked about it on the pod.
我们在播客里还没提过呢。

1085
00:46:32.840 --> 00:46:34.440
It was so amazing.
那场秀太棒了。

1086
00:46:34.860 --> 00:46:40.160
I mean, a lot of what was so amazing about it was just all of the really good best friend time that we had.
我是说，之所以那么棒，很大程度上是因为我们俩度过了非常美好的闺蜜时光。

1087
00:46:40.160 --> 00:46:43.360
I know I made a bunch of stories over at Office Ladies Pod.
我知道我在Office Ladies播客账号上发了很多故事。

1088
00:46:43.560 --> 00:46:44.720
I saved it as a highlight.
我还把它存成了精选。

1089
00:46:45.060 --> 00:46:48.820
But what a fun time to just go explore Vancouver a little bit.
能去温哥华稍微逛逛真是太开心了。

1090
00:46:49.660 --> 00:46:52.940
Well, during the show, there was a moment that took us both by surprise.
在演出期间，有一个瞬间让我们俩都感到意外。

1091
00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:54.760
I was not surprised by it.
我倒是一点都不意外。

1092
00:46:54.880 --> 00:46:55.380
You weren't?
你不意外？

1093
00:46:55.380 --> 00:46:56.900
You know what I'm talking about.
你知道我在说什么。

1094
00:46:57.260 --> 00:47:02.140
I remember I said, I said, listen, if we do this show in Texas, this moment's going to kill.
我记得我说过，听着，如果我们去德克萨斯办这场秀，这个梗绝对会炸场。

1095
00:47:02.320 --> 00:47:04.860
I'm not so sure about Vancouver.
在温哥华我就没那么确定了。

1096
00:47:05.620 --> 00:47:11.360
Well, during the show, we have a moment where we discuss Chunk It versus Chuck It.
演出时，我们讨论了“Chunk It”和“Chuck It”的用法。

1097
00:47:11.620 --> 00:47:11.900
Yeah.
没错。

1098
00:47:12.300 --> 00:47:18.320
And we asked the audience, almost 4,000 people in attendance, amazing crowd, lovely people.
我们问了现场观众，将近4000人，非常棒的观众，可爱的人们。

1099
00:47:18.320 --> 00:47:21.120
Well, do any of you say Chunk It?
你们有谁说“Chunk It”吗？

1100
00:47:21.540 --> 00:47:23.900
Not a single person.
一个人都没有。

1101
00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:27.680
No one in Vancouver says Chunk It.
温哥华根本没人说“Chunk It”。

1102
00:47:27.800 --> 00:47:29.620
And I was like, okay, okay.
当时我就想，好吧，好吧。

1103
00:47:29.980 --> 00:47:36.400
Well, I told you earlier that I went to our general mailbag this week, Angela, and I found this letter.
安吉拉，我之前跟你说过，这周我翻了翻我们的普通信箱，然后发现了这封信。

1104
00:47:36.720 --> 00:47:41.600
And in honor of that crickets moment at our Vancouver Live show.
为了纪念我们在温哥华现场演出时那段冷场的时刻。

1105
00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:43.080
It was so funny.
那真的太搞笑了。

1106
00:47:43.800 --> 00:47:45.900
I wanted to give you this gift.
我想送你这份礼物。

1107
00:47:46.040 --> 00:47:46.360
Okay.
好吧。

1108
00:47:46.360 --> 00:48:00.060
Via Madeline from Utah, who says, I was just watching Modern Family, and on Season 3, Episode 9, they say Chunk It.
来自犹他州的玛德琳说，我刚才在看《摩登家庭》，第三季第九集里，他们说了“Chunk It”。

1109
00:48:00.640 --> 00:48:01.400
No.
不会吧。

1110
00:48:01.780 --> 00:48:02.260
Yes.
真的。

1111
00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:07.720
In fact, the title of the episode is Punkin' Chunkin'.
事实上，那一集的标题就是《南瓜投掷大赛》（Punkin' Chunkin'）。

1112
00:48:07.720 --> 00:48:08.240
What?
什么？

1113
00:48:09.280 --> 00:48:18.160
In the episode, Cameron is trying to prove to the rest of his family that he used a slingshot to fling a pumpkin across a football field.
在那一集里，卡梅隆试图向家人们证明，他曾用弹弓把一个南瓜弹射过整个橄榄球场。

1114
00:48:18.500 --> 00:48:24.420
And in this episode, they all refer to this as Chunkin' the Pumpkin.
在这一集里，他们都把这称为“投掷南瓜”（Chunkin' the Pumpkin）。

1115
00:48:24.620 --> 00:48:25.060
Yes!
没错！

1116
00:48:25.560 --> 00:48:28.640
Madeline said, I just thought Angela would be so grateful.
玛德琳说，我只是觉得安吉拉一定会非常感激。

1117
00:48:28.640 --> 00:48:32.000
And Angela, I recorded this audio clip for you.
安吉拉，我为你录下了这段音频。

1118
00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:38.860
So, this is just one tiny moment from the episode where they repeatedly say Chunkin'.
这只是那一集里的一小段，他们反复提到了“Chunkin'”。

1119
00:48:38.860 --> 00:48:41.560
I'm just saying maybe you take Punkin' Chunkin' out of the rotation.
我只是说，也许你可以把“南瓜投掷大赛”从你的故事库里删掉。

1120
00:48:42.140 --> 00:48:42.840
I guess you're right.
我想你是对的。

1121
00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:43.520
Maybe I could juSt...
也许我可以……

1122
00:48:43.520 --> 00:48:45.860
You stick to the ones that really happened because people love those.
你还是坚持讲那些真实发生过的故事吧，因为大家很喜欢那些。

1123
00:48:46.640 --> 00:48:47.460
Excuse me, what?
抱歉，你说什么？

1124
00:48:48.040 --> 00:48:50.500
I'm just saying people laugh more at stories that are true.
我只是说，人们对真实的故事笑得更开心。

1125
00:48:50.840 --> 00:48:52.220
Punkin' Chunkin' is a true story.
“南瓜投掷大赛”是个真实的故事。

1126
00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:53.400
True-ish?
算是真实吧？

1127
00:48:53.840 --> 00:48:54.260
No.
不。

1128
00:48:54.940 --> 00:48:55.420
True.
就是真实的。

1129
00:48:55.880 --> 00:48:56.360
Really?
真的吗？

1130
00:48:57.220 --> 00:48:58.760
The length of a football field.
一个橄榄球场的长度。

1131
00:48:58.880 --> 00:49:03.160
Through the sunroof of a car that was opened in late November in Missouri.
穿过一辆在十一月下旬开着天窗的车，地点在密苏里州。

1132
00:49:03.420 --> 00:49:04.580
It was unseasonably warm.
当时天气异常温暖。

1133
00:49:04.900 --> 00:49:06.600
Explains of fog rolling over the hill.
解释了雾气如何翻过山丘。

1134
00:49:06.820 --> 00:49:07.600
And who's Cody?
还有，科迪是谁？

1135
00:49:07.820 --> 00:49:11.880
Who you're close enough to Chunk with, but mysteriously only appears in this story.
那个跟你关系好到能一起投掷南瓜，却神秘地只出现在这个故事里的人。

1136
00:49:12.080 --> 00:49:13.700
Cody was KIA in Desert Storm.
科迪在沙漠风暴行动中阵亡了。

1137
00:49:13.820 --> 00:49:14.360
He's a hero.
他是位英雄。

1138
00:49:15.120 --> 00:49:18.980
You know, all this from someone who's never even chunked a Punkin'.
你知道吗，这些话竟然出自一个从未投掷过南瓜的人之口。

1139
00:49:20.060 --> 00:49:21.680
I've never longed a Tonkin' either.
我也从来没去过东京（Tonkin'）。

1140
00:49:21.800 --> 00:49:23.000
You know, these aren't real things.
你知道，这些根本不是真实存在的东西。

1141
00:49:24.380 --> 00:49:25.500
There you go, Angela.
给你，安吉拉。

1142
00:49:25.800 --> 00:49:27.880
A whole episode of Chunkin' It!
整整一集都在说“Chunkin' It”！

1143
00:49:28.360 --> 00:49:31.180
Madeline, I want to thank you from the bottom of my heart.
玛德琳，我要从心底里感谢你。

1144
00:49:32.100 --> 00:49:38.640
You know, I know people say Chunkin' out there somewhere, but it was pretty amazing when 4,000 people were like, nope.
我知道外面确实有人会说“Chunkin'”，但当四千人异口同声说“没有”的时候，那种感觉真是太奇妙了。

1145
00:49:39.120 --> 00:49:43.420
I do want to say a big thank you to everyone at Just for Laughs Vancouver.
我确实想对温哥华“欢笑节”的所有人说声大大的感谢。

1146
00:49:43.420 --> 00:49:44.940
You guys were awesome.
你们太棒了。

1147
00:49:45.120 --> 00:49:46.480
Thank you to everyone who came out.
感谢所有到场的朋友。

1148
00:49:46.820 --> 00:49:53.920
And one thing, though, that happened with the Vancouver audience, which I thought was amazing, is I asked if anyone could speak Indonesian.
不过，在温哥华观众身上发生了一件我觉得很神奇的事，就是我问有没有人会说印尼语。

1149
00:49:53.940 --> 00:49:56.540
And there were several people that could speak Indonesian.
结果有好几个人都会说印尼语。

1150
00:49:56.720 --> 00:49:58.160
I was so thrilled.
我当时太激动了。

1151
00:49:58.260 --> 00:49:59.620
And I yelled out to them.
我当时冲他们大喊。

1152
00:49:59.700 --> 00:50:01.020
And we had a moment.
我们当时心领神会。

1153
00:50:01.020 --> 00:50:04.100
You know, we're really excited to keep doing more of these live shows.
你知道，我们真的很兴奋能继续做更多的现场演出。

1154
00:50:04.300 --> 00:50:09.240
We had to put them on pause for a hot second because I got that part in the Mean Girls movie musical.
我们不得不暂停了一小会儿，因为我接到了电影版《贱女孩》音乐剧里的那个角色。

1155
00:50:09.500 --> 00:50:13.540
But we are okay to hit the pause button because we are so excited for you to be in this movie.
但我们愿意按下暂停键，因为我们为你参演这部电影感到无比兴奋。

1156
00:50:13.700 --> 00:50:18.140
And I can't wait to share about it, but we're not really supposed to share any details.
我迫不及待想分享这件事，但我们其实不被允许透露任何细节。

1157
00:50:18.580 --> 00:50:18.880
All right.
好吧。

1158
00:50:18.980 --> 00:50:20.600
You've got to give us some nuggets, lady.
你得给我们透点料，女士。

1159
00:50:20.860 --> 00:50:21.200
All right.
好吧。

1160
00:50:21.300 --> 00:50:22.740
I'll see what I can share.
我看看能分享些什么。

1161
00:50:22.780 --> 00:50:23.040
Okay.
好的。

1162
00:50:23.040 --> 00:50:24.240
In a future episode.
在以后的剧集里吧。

1163
00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:33.040
So, like we said before we went to break, Kelly is now a member of the search committee because Gabe is heading back to Florida.
就像我们在休息前说的那样，凯莉现在是搜寻委员会的一员了，因为盖博要回佛罗里达了。

1164
00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:36.540
The first person that they're going to interview now is Dwight.
他们现在要面试的第一个人是德怀特。

1165
00:50:36.960 --> 00:50:40.320
Well, actually, Dwight is going to interview Dwight in front of them.
嗯，实际上，是德怀特要在他们面前面试德怀特自己。

1166
00:50:40.460 --> 00:50:41.900
And he did a really good job.
而且他表现得非常好。

1167
00:50:42.040 --> 00:50:45.640
I mean, he kind of convinced Toby and Kelly that he should have a shot.
我是说，他算是说服了托比和凯莉，让他们觉得他应该有机会。

1168
00:50:45.640 --> 00:50:53.340
We got a fan catch from British Columbia, Canada, who says, I'm 10 years old and you're my favorite podcast by far.
我们收到了一位来自加拿大不列颠哥伦比亚省粉丝的发现，他说：我今年10岁，你们是我最喜欢的播客，遥遥领先。

1169
00:50:53.340 --> 00:50:55.580
And I have a continuity catch.
我有一个关于连贯性的发现。

1170
00:50:55.800 --> 00:50:56.720
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1171
00:50:56.940 --> 00:51:03.340
When Kelly, Toby and Jim are conducting interviews for the manager position, Kelly's nails are painted white.
当凯莉、托比和吉姆在进行经理职位的面试时，凯莉的指甲涂的是白色的。

1172
00:51:03.660 --> 00:51:09.720
But when they're in the bullpen discussing if Dwight should be made manager, her nails are now green.
但当他们在办公区讨论是否应该让德怀特当经理时，她的指甲变成了绿色。

1173
00:51:10.360 --> 00:51:10.860
Oh.
哦。

1174
00:51:11.440 --> 00:51:13.360
Lemon, this is such a good catch.
柠檬，这发现太棒了。

1175
00:51:13.680 --> 00:51:13.900
Yes.
没错。

1176
00:51:13.900 --> 00:51:16.660
So, go to 10 minutes, 35 seconds.
所以，去看10分35秒处。

1177
00:51:16.900 --> 00:51:21.580
There is only one shot in the entire conference room where you actually see her nails.
在整个会议室的镜头里，只有一个镜头能真正看清她的指甲。

1178
00:51:21.580 --> 00:51:24.320
So, that is how detail-oriented this catch is.
所以，这个发现的细节关注度有多高可见一斑。

1179
00:51:24.520 --> 00:51:27.880
It's at 10 minutes and 35 seconds when she crosses her arMs.
就在10分35秒，她交叉双臂的时候。

1180
00:51:28.160 --> 00:51:32.500
But then at 12 minutes and 3 seconds, she is standing behind Dwight in the bullpen.
但到了12分03秒，她站在办公区的德怀特身后。

1181
00:51:32.580 --> 00:51:37.600
And she has her hands on the file cabinet right by the Froggy 101 sticker.
她的手放在Froggy 101贴纸旁边的文件柜上。

1182
00:51:37.720 --> 00:51:39.880
And her nails are very green.
她的指甲非常绿。

1183
00:51:40.180 --> 00:51:41.380
What a great catch.
真是个伟大的发现。

1184
00:51:42.240 --> 00:51:45.280
Well, pretty quickly, Jim realizes that Kelly took the deal.
嗯，吉姆很快就意识到凯莉接受了那个交易。

1185
00:51:45.760 --> 00:51:48.520
She has the same quote, that quote about...
她引用了同样的话，那句关于……

1186
00:51:48.520 --> 00:51:52.520
Oh, the ham that comes out of the grave and grips around your neck is the one you want on the steering wheel.
哦，从坟墓里爬出来掐住你脖子的火腿，才是你想要握在方向盘上的那一个。

1187
00:51:52.780 --> 00:51:53.180
Bingo.
答对了。

1188
00:51:53.440 --> 00:51:53.600
Right.
没错。

1189
00:51:53.600 --> 00:51:55.780
So, Jim's like, you took the deal.
所以吉姆就说，你接受了交易。

1190
00:51:56.380 --> 00:51:58.900
But then Toby is also agreeing with her.
但随后托比也同意她的观点。

1191
00:51:59.340 --> 00:52:00.840
Jim is like, what is happening now?
吉姆心想，现在到底发生了什么？

1192
00:52:01.120 --> 00:52:07.640
Then Phyllis storms into the conference room and says that Dwight and Kelly told her that Dwight is the manager and they pre-fired her.
然后菲利斯冲进会议室，说德怀特和凯莉告诉她德怀特是经理，而且他们已经预先解雇了她。

1193
00:52:08.460 --> 00:52:14.540
So, this is going to lead to an epic bullpen scene that is very long and very complex.
所以，这将引出一段非常长且非常复杂的史诗级办公区场景。

1194
00:52:14.540 --> 00:52:18.240
And every character gets to have a line here or a line there.
每个角色在这里都能插上一两句台词。

1195
00:52:18.360 --> 00:52:19.640
And I absolutely loved it.
我绝对喜欢这个场景。

1196
00:52:19.740 --> 00:52:21.560
It felt very classic office to me.
我觉得这非常有《办公室》的经典味道。

1197
00:52:21.780 --> 00:52:24.840
Miles McNutt pointed it out in his review as well.
迈尔斯·麦克纳特在他的评论中也指出了这一点。

1198
00:52:24.980 --> 00:52:25.140
Thank you, Miles.
谢谢你，迈尔斯。

1199
00:52:25.140 --> 00:52:28.080
So, I feel like we've got a little same brain thing happening.
所以，我觉得我们有点心有灵犀了。

1200
00:52:28.840 --> 00:52:33.400
Well, basically, the whole entire bullpen is going to weigh in on who they think should be the manager.
嗯，基本上，整个办公区的人都要对他们认为谁应该当经理发表意见。

1201
00:52:33.860 --> 00:52:33.960
Yeah.
没错。

1202
00:52:34.240 --> 00:52:35.540
Jim has lost the room.
吉姆已经无法掌控全场了。

1203
00:52:35.800 --> 00:52:37.500
Very quickly loses the room.
很快就失去了对全场的掌控。

1204
00:52:38.040 --> 00:52:39.840
Kevin talks for a bit.
凯文说了一会儿话。

1205
00:52:40.040 --> 00:52:42.940
He's tickled because he has everyone's attention, but he has nothing to say.
他因为吸引了所有人的注意而感到沾沾自喜，但他其实没什么可说的。

1206
00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:44.300
They shoo him off.
大家把他轰走了。

1207
00:52:44.380 --> 00:52:46.860
They're like, you can only speak if you have something to contribute.
他们就像是在说，只有你有话要说的时候才能发言。

1208
00:52:47.280 --> 00:52:50.020
And Ryan says, I want an outsider.
然后瑞安说，我想要个局外人。

1209
00:52:50.560 --> 00:52:52.200
Like a homeless person.
比如流浪汉之类的。

1210
00:52:52.580 --> 00:52:55.720
This is a really delicious Ryan Pam moment.
这真是瑞安和帕姆之间非常精彩的时刻。

1211
00:52:56.580 --> 00:52:58.520
I loved these so much.
我太喜欢这些时刻了。

1212
00:52:58.660 --> 00:53:00.020
Pam says, a homeless person?
帕姆说，流浪汉？

1213
00:53:00.100 --> 00:53:00.360
Really?
真的吗？

1214
00:53:00.820 --> 00:53:01.300
No.
不。

1215
00:53:01.440 --> 00:53:06.360
I want you to say that you think the best person to be our new manager is a homeless person.
我要你说出你认为最适合担任我们新经理的人选就是个流浪汉。

1216
00:53:06.620 --> 00:53:08.420
And Ryan's like, let me guess who you want, Pam.
然后瑞安就像是说，让我猜猜你想要谁，帕姆。

1217
00:53:08.620 --> 00:53:09.340
Rachel Ray?
瑞秋·雷？

1218
00:53:09.600 --> 00:53:10.880
The ladies of the view?
《观点》节目的那些女士们？

1219
00:53:11.500 --> 00:53:11.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1220
00:53:12.360 --> 00:53:12.660
Yeah.
没错。

1221
00:53:12.960 --> 00:53:19.340
Then Ryan has a talking head where he says he got away with everything under the last boss and it wasn't good for him.
然后瑞安有个单人访谈，他说他在上一任老板手下时什么坏事都干过，这对他的成长没好处。

1222
00:53:19.660 --> 00:53:21.580
He wants guidance and leadership.
他想要指导和领导。

1223
00:53:21.940 --> 00:53:24.880
But, you know, when he's in the mood to be led.
但是，你知道的，得在他心情好愿意被领导的时候。

1224
00:53:24.880 --> 00:53:26.080
Yeah, don't boss him around.
没错，别对他指手画脚。

1225
00:53:26.260 --> 00:53:26.460
No.
没错。

1226
00:53:26.840 --> 00:53:28.680
We had a fan question from Aaron G.
我们收到了一位来自俄亥俄州哥伦布市的粉丝亚伦·G的提问。

1227
00:53:28.820 --> 00:53:29.700
in Columbus, Ohio.
在俄亥俄州的哥伦布市。

1228
00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:31.720
I found this very interesting.
我觉得这非常有趣。

1229
00:53:32.060 --> 00:53:32.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1230
00:53:32.720 --> 00:53:39.460
Aaron said, was there a rule or contractual agreement that you could not use the name Michael after Steve Carell left?
亚伦问，是不是有什么规定或合同协议，导致史蒂夫·卡瑞尔离开后你们就不能再用迈克尔这个名字了？

1231
00:53:39.640 --> 00:53:40.000
What?
什么？

1232
00:53:40.320 --> 00:53:41.100
I know.
我知道。

1233
00:53:41.300 --> 00:53:50.160
Aaron said, unless I'm mistaken, for the remainder of the episodes of season seven and up to almost the end of season nine, Michael's name is not used or referenced.
亚伦说，如果我没记错的话，在第七季剩下的剧集里，一直到第九季快结束，迈克尔的名字都没有被提及或使用过。

1234
00:53:50.980 --> 00:53:59.040
And in this talking head, Ryan says, I got away with everything under the last boss, which I thought was kind of odd.
而在那个单人访谈里，瑞安说，我在上一任老板手下时什么坏事都干过，我觉得这有点奇怪。

1235
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:04.680
After that, I started paying attention and noticed that no one says the name Michael again until season nine.
在那之后，我开始留意，并注意到直到第九季为止，再也没有人提到过迈克尔这个名字。

1236
00:54:05.100 --> 00:54:07.680
Okay, well, I definitely don't think that was intentional.
好吧，我绝对不认为那是故意的。

1237
00:54:07.880 --> 00:54:10.960
In fact, I have found in deleted scenes when his name was said.
事实上，我在删减片段里发现过提到他名字的地方。

1238
00:54:11.200 --> 00:54:14.620
Remember, Jim and Pam have a joint talking head that was in deleted scenes.
记得吗，吉姆和帕姆有个合拍的单人访谈就在删减片段里。

1239
00:54:14.760 --> 00:54:14.840
Yeah.
没错。

1240
00:54:14.920 --> 00:54:18.780
When we find out that Michael adopted a dog and named it...
当时我们发现迈克尔领养了一只狗，并给它取名叫……

1241
00:54:18.780 --> 00:54:19.520
Pam Beaksley.
帕姆·比克斯利。

1242
00:54:19.640 --> 00:54:20.380
Pam Beaksley.
帕姆·比克斯利。

1243
00:54:20.500 --> 00:54:21.160
And it's a beagle.
而且那是一只比格犬。

1244
00:54:21.480 --> 00:54:21.780
Yeah.
没错。

1245
00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:24.220
So, I think that is so crazy.
所以，我觉得这太疯狂了。

1246
00:54:24.360 --> 00:54:25.820
I'm going to start paying attention to that, though.
不过，我打算开始关注这一点了。

1247
00:54:25.920 --> 00:54:26.080
Me, too.
我也是。

1248
00:54:26.440 --> 00:54:27.020
New tracker.
新的追踪目标。

1249
00:54:27.500 --> 00:54:30.160
Well, Meredith has a request for the next branch manager.
嗯，梅雷迪思对下一任分公司经理有个要求。

1250
00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:36.880
She wants this person to be smart, professional, decisive, well-hung, and in his 40s.
她希望这个人聪明、专业、果断、那方面能力强，而且四十多岁。

1251
00:54:37.260 --> 00:54:38.660
And Jim's like, hey, hey, hey.
然后吉姆就说，嘿，嘿，嘿。

1252
00:54:39.100 --> 00:54:42.360
And then she's like, fine, hire the guy with a small penis.
接着她说，行吧，那就雇那个小丁丁的家伙好了。

1253
00:54:42.980 --> 00:54:43.940
Andy chimes in.
安迪插话道。

1254
00:54:44.060 --> 00:54:45.660
He says, would that work for you?
他说，那样对你有用吗？

1255
00:54:45.800 --> 00:54:47.180
Like a small to moderate penis.
就像那种小到中等尺寸的丁丁。

1256
00:54:47.400 --> 00:54:48.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1257
00:54:48.420 --> 00:54:49.400
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1258
00:54:49.540 --> 00:54:50.860
It was so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

1259
00:54:50.860 --> 00:54:52.520
Ed's delivery on that is perfection.
埃德那段台词的演绎简直完美。

1260
00:54:52.780 --> 00:54:53.460
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

1261
00:54:54.180 --> 00:54:56.380
This is when Gabe is going to leave.
这是盖博要离开的时候。

1262
00:54:57.460 --> 00:54:57.860
Sorry.
抱歉。

1263
00:54:58.320 --> 00:54:59.560
Sorry, it makes me laugh.
抱歉，这让我忍不住想笑。

1264
00:54:59.720 --> 00:54:59.840
I know.
我知道。

1265
00:54:59.880 --> 00:55:04.260
Because I'm imagining Kelly's reaction when she hugs him, and it's just so funny.
因为我在想象凯莉拥抱他时的反应，真的太搞笑了。

1266
00:55:04.440 --> 00:55:05.700
She says, ew.
她说，咦。

1267
00:55:05.760 --> 00:55:07.720
And he goes, you don't have to make that noise.
然后他说，你没必要发出那种声音。

1268
00:55:07.740 --> 00:55:10.860
And she said, he was just so much bonier than I thought.
她说，他比我想象中要瘦骨嶙峋得多。

1269
00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:12.060
There's so many more bones.
骨头也太多了。

1270
00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:18.400
When Gabe left, as I was watching it, I thought, this group of people can't wait to have a cake,
当盖博离开时，我看着那一幕心想，这群人真是迫不及待想吃蛋糕，

1271
00:55:18.560 --> 00:55:20.040
a party, for any reason.
想开派对，不管什么理由都行。

1272
00:55:20.040 --> 00:55:22.000
And they literally are like, oh, what?
他们简直就像是，哦，什么？

1273
00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:22.400
You're leaving?
你要走了？

1274
00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:22.840
Okay, bye.
好吧，再见。

1275
00:55:23.400 --> 00:55:24.080
I know.
我知道。

1276
00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:27.680
And you can't even use the excuse that it all came down in one day.
而且你甚至不能用“一切发生得太突然”来当借口。

1277
00:55:28.140 --> 00:55:31.400
Although maybe you can use the excuse that it's because Michael wasn't there.
虽然也许你可以用“因为迈克尔不在”来当借口。

1278
00:55:31.740 --> 00:55:36.360
Because even if someone's leaving in three hours, Michael's going to find a way to have
因为即使有人三个小时后就要走，迈克尔也会想方设法

1279
00:55:36.360 --> 00:55:37.240
it to do about it.
搞出点动静来。

1280
00:55:37.360 --> 00:55:37.520
Right.
没错。

1281
00:55:37.520 --> 00:55:41.300
So things have changed, especially when they're Gabe.
所以情况变了，尤其是当主角是盖博的时候。

1282
00:55:42.200 --> 00:55:45.320
Jim is going to suggest Daryl again.
吉姆又要提议达里尔了。

1283
00:55:45.700 --> 00:55:48.920
And this is when Angela decides to join the conversation.
这时候安吉拉决定加入对话。

1284
00:55:49.540 --> 00:55:52.180
She says, well, let me be clear.
她说，好吧，我得把话说清楚。

1285
00:55:52.320 --> 00:55:56.680
I only speak for myself and not myself and the senator.
我只代表我自己，不代表我和参议员。

1286
00:55:57.160 --> 00:56:02.060
I think we have some wonderful candidates and there's a great, lively debate here.
我认为我们有一些很棒的候选人，这里正在进行一场精彩而热烈的辩论。

1287
00:56:02.220 --> 00:56:03.620
But let's think about...
但让我们考虑一下……

1288
00:56:03.620 --> 00:56:05.000
And Toby goes, no, no, no.
然后托比说，不，不，不。

1289
00:56:05.140 --> 00:56:06.020
We did this with Kevin.
我们在凯文身上已经试过一次了。

1290
00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:08.360
If you have nothing to say, stop talking.
如果你没什么可说的，就闭嘴。

1291
00:56:09.040 --> 00:56:09.860
So here's the thing.
所以重点是这样的。

1292
00:56:09.920 --> 00:56:14.300
When we started filming this scene, I talked to Paul and our director, Jeff Blitz, and
当我们开始拍摄这场戏时，我和保罗还有我们的导演杰夫·布里茨聊过，

1293
00:56:14.300 --> 00:56:19.020
we had this idea that it would be really fun if Angela is already seeing herself as the
我们有个想法，如果安吉拉已经把自己看作参议员夫人，并且像是在竞选拉票一样，那会很有趣。

1294
00:56:19.020 --> 00:56:21.460
senator's wife and she's like on the campaign trail.
所以她在练习竞选演讲，但她决定就在这里试一试。

1295
00:56:21.460 --> 00:56:27.520
So she's practicing her campaign speeches, but she just decides to try it out right here.
一旦他们给了我这个指导，就变得太有趣了。

1296
00:56:27.820 --> 00:56:31.320
And once they gave me that note, it was so much fun.
我迫不及待地想说出这些台词。

1297
00:56:31.520 --> 00:56:34.000
I couldn't wait to deliver these lines.
作为演员，我喜欢那种能得到好建议的时候。

1298
00:56:34.240 --> 00:56:36.380
I love as an actor when you get a good note.
没错。

1299
00:56:36.660 --> 00:56:37.020
Yeah.
这对我来说改变了整个演讲的基调。

1300
00:56:37.380 --> 00:56:39.340
It changed the whole speech for me.
这对我来说改变了整个演讲的基调。

1301
00:56:39.340 --> 00:56:40.680
It opens up your whole performance.
这会让你的整体表现大放异彩。

1302
00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:43.540
Lady, we got a fan mail flurry.
女士，我们收到了一大波粉丝来信。

1303
00:56:44.200 --> 00:56:48.360
It's really been a while since we've had such a flurry of mail on a single subject.
真的好久没收到过针对单一主题的这么多来信了。

1304
00:56:48.520 --> 00:56:49.620
And it was this.
而主题就是这个。

1305
00:56:49.620 --> 00:56:52.540
Why doesn't Jim step in as manager?
为什么吉姆不接手当经理呢？

1306
00:56:52.860 --> 00:56:56.180
Why was he not considered or interviewed for the position?
为什么他没有被考虑或面试这个职位？

1307
00:56:56.700 --> 00:56:58.120
He didn't want to be.
他自己不想当。

1308
00:56:58.300 --> 00:57:00.760
He didn't want to be interim manager.
他不想当临时经理。

1309
00:57:01.220 --> 00:57:09.320
But of everyone in the office besides Daryl, Jim is our other most sober, most qualified
但除了达里尔，吉姆是我们办公室里最稳重、最合格的

1310
00:57:09.320 --> 00:57:09.940
candidate.
候选人。

1311
00:57:10.540 --> 00:57:12.240
It is sort of a why.
这确实是个疑问。

1312
00:57:12.460 --> 00:57:17.940
Why doesn't he want a promotion with more money and more financial stability for his family?
为什么他不想升职，不想为家人争取更多的钱和财务保障呢？

1313
00:57:18.160 --> 00:57:19.100
Why doesn't he want that?
为什么他不想呢？

1314
00:57:19.620 --> 00:57:21.360
I agree with this fan mail flurry.
我同意这波粉丝来信的观点。

1315
00:57:21.580 --> 00:57:22.100
I don't know.
我不知道。

1316
00:57:22.460 --> 00:57:28.040
I think that the honest answer to this question is that they had no intention of making the
我觉得这个问题的诚实答案是，他们根本没打算让吉姆这个

1317
00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:35.960
character of Jim the manager because the show isn't served by having a qualified, sober-minded
角色当经理，因为如果有一个合格、头脑清醒的经理，

1318
00:57:35.960 --> 00:57:36.520
manager.
这剧就没法演了。

1319
00:57:37.120 --> 00:57:42.480
The whole show depends on having a branch manager that everyone doesn't like or has to deal with.
整部剧都靠一个大家都不喜欢或者必须应付的分公司经理来支撑。

1320
00:57:42.840 --> 00:57:43.040
Correct.
没错。

1321
00:57:43.460 --> 00:57:46.940
Well, they're going to have to go back to the conference room now to figure this out.
好了，他们现在得回会议室去商量这件事了。

1322
00:57:47.240 --> 00:57:52.440
Did any of you guys notice that Brian as Kevin follows them back in the conference room and they
你们有没有注意到布莱恩饰演的凯文跟着他们进了会议室，然后他们

1323
00:57:52.440 --> 00:57:53.540
shut the door in his face?
把门关上，把他挡在外面了？

1324
00:57:53.740 --> 00:57:54.000
Yes.
看到了。

1325
00:57:54.420 --> 00:57:55.740
Brian improvised that.
那是布莱恩即兴发挥的。

1326
00:57:55.740 --> 00:57:56.640
Oh, that's funny.
哦，那太搞笑了。

1327
00:57:56.820 --> 00:58:00.540
I totally remember him doing it in the moment and I was cracking up because I was like,
我完全记得他当时那么做，我当时都要笑死了，因为我在想，

1328
00:58:00.600 --> 00:58:01.220
where's he going?
他要去哪儿？

1329
00:58:02.100 --> 00:58:04.540
Well, we're going to have a series of talking heads.
好了，接下来会有一系列访谈片段。

1330
00:58:04.940 --> 00:58:10.480
First of all, Phyllis is going to let us know that she got the call from the, I guess,
首先，菲利斯会告诉我们她接到了，我猜是，

1331
00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.400
DNA offices or adoption agency.
DNA鉴定中心或者领养机构的电话。

1332
00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:14.520
You know, the DNA offices.
你知道的，就是DNA鉴定中心。

1333
00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:14.940
You know.
你懂的。

1334
00:58:15.020 --> 00:58:16.000
They're by the DMV.
就在车管所旁边。

1335
00:58:16.240 --> 00:58:19.780
It's like post office, DMV, the DNA office.
就像邮局、车管所、DNA鉴定中心那样。

1336
00:58:20.340 --> 00:58:20.520
Exactly.
没错。

1337
00:58:20.860 --> 00:58:24.360
Well, they called and she and Erin are not related.
他们打电话来说，她和艾琳没有血缘关系。

1338
00:58:24.620 --> 00:58:26.260
But she's going to tell her another day.
但她打算改天再告诉艾琳。

1339
00:58:26.700 --> 00:58:26.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1340
00:58:27.100 --> 00:58:27.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1341
00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:30.820
They've been enjoying, I guess, this idea that maybe Phyllis is her mom.
她们一直很享受这种猜测，觉得菲利斯可能是她妈妈。

1342
00:58:31.260 --> 00:58:37.360
And she also encouraged Erin to really go for Andy and Erin did it with a sock puppet
而且她还鼓励艾琳勇敢去追安迪，结果艾琳用袜子木偶表白，

1343
00:58:37.360 --> 00:58:38.960
and was told no in front of everyone.
当着所有人的面被拒绝了。

1344
00:58:38.960 --> 00:58:42.800
So maybe not the best day to get additional bad news.
所以这可能不是告诉她更多坏消息的好日子。

1345
00:58:43.400 --> 00:58:44.240
Good point.
有道理。

1346
00:58:44.880 --> 00:58:51.020
The episode ends with a bunch of talking heads from all the various candidates about, you
这一集最后是一连串各路候选人的访谈片段，谈论他们

1347
00:58:51.020 --> 00:58:54.480
know, whether or not they think they're going to get this job as the manager.
是否觉得自己能得到经理这个职位。

1348
00:58:54.940 --> 00:58:57.300
They end with Finger Lakes guy.
最后是那个“手指湖”哥们儿。

1349
00:58:57.560 --> 00:59:01.700
We finally meet the guy who was so worried about getting the first two weeks off work
我们终于见到了那个一直担心请不到前两周假

1350
00:59:01.700 --> 00:59:02.640
to go to the Finger Lakes.
去手指湖度假的家伙。

1351
00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:03.880
And it's Jim Carrey.
而且是金·凯瑞。

1352
00:59:04.520 --> 00:59:08.780
Brent Forrester was the person in charge of reaching out to Jim Carrey's reps.
布伦特·福雷斯特负责联系金·凯瑞的经纪人。

1353
00:59:08.780 --> 00:59:12.760
Brent said that Jim Carrey was an enthusiastic yes.
布伦特说金·凯瑞非常爽快地答应了。

1354
00:59:13.100 --> 00:59:18.120
And incidentally, Jim Carrey received a nomination for favorite TV guest star at the
顺便提一下，金·凯瑞凭借这次客串获得了

1355
00:59:18.120 --> 00:59:20.820
38th People's Choice Awards for this cameo.
第38届人民选择奖最受欢迎电视客串明星的提名。

1356
00:59:20.980 --> 00:59:22.320
Aw, for Finger Lakes guy?
噢，是因为“手指湖”那个人吗？

1357
00:59:22.340 --> 00:59:23.600
For Finger Lakes guy.
就是“手指湖”那个人。

1358
00:59:24.040 --> 00:59:27.220
So fun that we got all of these cool guest stars for this episode.
这一集能请到这么多酷炫的客串明星真是太有趣了。

1359
00:59:27.220 --> 00:59:28.980
It really made it fun to rewatch.
重温的时候真的很有意思。

1360
00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:32.840
Well, we have one final moment with Creed as branch manager.
好了，我们来看看克里德担任分部经理的最后一个片段。

1361
00:59:32.840 --> 00:59:35.480
He's talking to his ninth biggest client.
他正在和他的第九大客户通话。

1362
00:59:36.140 --> 00:59:37.060
It's Pam.
是帕姆。

1363
00:59:37.620 --> 00:59:38.060
Yes.
没错。

1364
00:59:38.320 --> 00:59:42.940
And he thinks the ninth biggest client and his fourth biggest client would get along.
他觉得他的第九大客户和第四大客户会聊得来。

1365
00:59:42.980 --> 00:59:44.980
And now they have to all talk to each other.
现在他们都得互相通话了。

1366
00:59:45.360 --> 00:59:45.960
Yes.
是的。

1367
00:59:46.400 --> 00:59:50.900
So one of my favorite moments in this little bit, I improvised.
在这个小片段里，我最喜欢的一个瞬间是我即兴发挥的。

1368
00:59:51.860 --> 00:59:54.800
There's the moment when, you know, he says,
就是那个瞬间，你知道，他说，

1369
00:59:55.160 --> 00:59:58.260
Hey, Jordan, patch through my fourth biggest client.
嘿，乔丹，帮我接通我的第四大客户。

1370
00:59:58.800 --> 01:00:02.080
And I move the phone across my keyboard.
然后我把电话在键盘上划过去。

1371
01:00:02.480 --> 01:00:05.400
That was like, that's the patching through sound.
那就像是接通电话的声音。

1372
01:00:05.740 --> 01:00:07.560
That was a little bit I came up with.
那是我自己想出来的小花招。

1373
01:00:07.900 --> 01:00:08.500
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

1374
01:00:08.660 --> 01:00:13.220
And then I got to perform both sides of the conversation, which was, I mean, it delighted me.
然后我还能分饰两角进行对话，我是说，这让我乐在其中。

1375
01:00:13.680 --> 01:00:15.660
Well, I don't know if anyone else caught it.
嗯，我不知道有没有人注意到。

1376
01:00:15.940 --> 01:00:20.140
But remember how Creed said he would intentionally say people's names wrong on purpose,
还记得克里德说过他会故意把别人的名字叫错吗，

1377
01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:22.180
even if they were written correctly in the script?
即使剧本里写得清清楚楚？

1378
01:00:22.380 --> 01:00:22.640
Yes.
记得。

1379
01:00:22.980 --> 01:00:24.960
Well, in this scene, he called Jordan,
在这个场景里，他管乔丹叫，

1380
01:00:25.340 --> 01:00:25.880
Jordana.
乔丹娜。

1381
01:00:26.260 --> 01:00:26.960
Oh, nice.
噢，不错。

1382
01:00:28.220 --> 01:00:32.300
Well, we should say that this is going to end Creed's stint as manager.
我们得说，这将是克里德经理生涯的终点。

1383
01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:35.640
And we'll also be saying goodbye to Cody Horn, who played Jordan.
我们也要和饰演乔丹的科迪·霍恩说再见了。

1384
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:37.340
She does not return in season eight.
她不会在第八季回归。

1385
01:00:37.660 --> 01:00:40.960
But a lot of new stuff does happen in season eight.
但第八季确实会发生很多新鲜事。

1386
01:00:41.080 --> 01:00:43.880
And I cannot wait to break down the liSt.
我迫不及待想剖析一下清单了。

1387
01:00:44.140 --> 01:00:45.240
Oh, I can't wait.
噢，我也等不及了。

1388
01:00:45.440 --> 01:00:48.800
Before we get to season eight, we had a fun idea, you guys.
在进入第八季之前，我们有个好主意，各位。

1389
01:00:48.800 --> 01:00:52.920
We think it is time to break down a Keanu Reeves movie.
我们觉得是时候剖析一部基努·里维斯的电影了。

1390
01:00:53.420 --> 01:00:55.220
And we're going to start with speed.
我们要从《生死时速》开始。

1391
01:00:55.220 --> 01:00:59.780
Yes, a little palate cleanser between season seven and season eight.
没错，在第七季和第八季之间来点清口小菜。

1392
01:00:59.960 --> 01:01:01.720
Next week, we're breaking down speed.
下周，我们将剖析《生死时速》。

1393
01:01:02.060 --> 01:01:06.980
So tune in next week to hear us talk about Keanu Reeves and everything about that big old bus.
所以下周记得收听，听我们聊聊基努·里维斯和那辆大巴士的一切。

1394
01:01:06.980 --> 01:01:09.400
And thank you guys so much for listening today.
非常感谢大家今天的收听。

1395
01:01:09.640 --> 01:01:12.700
And a big thank you to Rainn Wilson, who came into this studio.
还要特别感谢来到演播室的雷恩·威尔森。

1396
01:01:13.720 --> 01:01:16.440
Just what a special person.
他真是个特别的人。

1397
01:01:16.680 --> 01:01:17.360
Thank you, Rainn.
谢谢你，雷恩。

1398
01:01:17.420 --> 01:01:17.900
We love you.
我们爱你。

1399
01:01:18.040 --> 01:01:18.560
Love you.
爱你。

1400
01:01:18.800 --> 01:01:19.560
